                                                          |     |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --- |\n| Content provider data leak | `entry` provider lines (`content query --uri …`) — note `exported=false` + `grantUriPermissions=true` needs a grant | ~   |","table":"table-5"},"140":{"id":"/docs/checklist#49","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#6-runtime-components-and-injection","content":"| Check                       | Command                                                                      |     |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --- |\n| Task hijacking / StrandHogg | needs a real launcher and a second malicious app — out of scope for this rig | ✘   |","table":"table-5"},"141":{"id":"/docs/checklist#50","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#6-runtime-components-and-injection","content":"| Check                        | Command                                                                   |     |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --- |\n| Tapjacking / overlay attacks | needs overlay permissions and a real UI; emulator OK but no template here | ✘   |","table":"table-5"},"142":{"id":"/docs/checklist#51","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#6-runtime-components-and-injection","content":"| Check                   | Command                                |     |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------- | --- |\n| Dynamic instrumentation | `fspawn <pkg> trace\\|attest\\|web\\|spy` | ✔   |","table":"table-5"},"143":{"id":"/docs/checklist#52","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#6-runtime-components-and-injection","content":"| Check                       | Command                                                               |     |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | --- |\n| Root/emulator checks firing | `fspawn <pkg> trace` → `30-rootcheck.js` prints each path/API queried | ✔   |","table":"table-5"},"144":{"id":"/docs/checklist#53","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#7-server-side-where-the-money-usually-is","content":"| Check              | Command                                          |     |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ | --- |\n| Endpoint inventory | `flows` index + `recon --deep` endpoints, diffed | ✔   |","table":"table-6"},"145":{"id":"/docs/checklist#54","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#7-server-side-where-the-money-usually-is","content":"| Check                   | Command                          |     |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------- | --- |\n| Authz: object ownership | `replay` with another user's ids | ✔   |","table":"table-6"},"146":{"id":"/docs/checklist#55","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#7-server-side-where-the-money-usually-is","content":"| Check                             | Command          |     |\n| --------------------------------- | ---------------- | --- |\n| Mass assignment / field injection | `replay --patch` | ✔   |","table":"table-6"},"147":{"id":"/docs/checklist#56","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#7-server-side-where-the-money-usually-is","content":"| Check                 | Command                                |     |\n| --------------------- | -------------------------------------- | --- |\n| Rate limits / lockout | `replay` in a loop, watch status codes | ✔   |","table":"table-6"},"148":{"id":"/docs/checklist#57","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#7-server-side-where-the-money-usually-is","content":"| Check          | Command                                                                      |     |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --- |\n| MFA weaknesses | `session harvest` → inspect `/auth/session`-style endpoints for seeds/tokens | ✔   |","table":"table-6"},"149":{"id":"/docs/checklist#58","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#7-server-side-where-the-money-usually-is","content":"| Check                         | Command                                    |     |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | --- |\n| Logout / session invalidation | `replay` the logout, then reuse the cookie | ✔   |","table":"table-6"},"150":{"id":"/docs/checklist#59","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#8-what-this-rig-cannot-tell-you","content":"Anything hardware-backed that you did not spoof: sensors, Secure Element, StrongBox, real TEE behaviour."},"151":{"id":"/docs/checklist#60","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#8-what-this-rig-cannot-tell-you","content":"Play Integrity verdicts (why)."},"152":{"id":"/docs/checklist#61","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#8-what-this-rig-cannot-tell-you","content":"Bluetooth, NFC, USB, SIM/telephony behaviour."},"153":{"id":"/docs/checklist#62","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#8-what-this-rig-cannot-tell-you","content":"OEM-specific bugs (the emulator is AOSP + Google image, no vendor blobs)."},"154":{"id":"/docs/checklist#63","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#8-what-this-rig-cannot-tell-you","content":"Performance/timing side channels that depend on real CPU and memory pressure."},"155":{"id":"/docs/checklist#64","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#8-what-this-rig-cannot-tell-you","content":"Whether a leaked key matters — that is a server-side validation question, and the answer changes per target."},"156":{"id":"/docs/checklist#65","page_id":"/docs/checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/checklist#reporting-habit","content":"For every finding, keep the evidence triple: **the flow file** (`/tmp/mtflows/…txt`), **the replay command** that reproduces it, and **the app state** (which `snap` image, which user, which Frida profile). `_index.jsonl` plus a one-line `replay` command is the cheapest possible repro packet."},"157":{"id":"/docs/flows","page_id":"/docs/flows","type":"page","content":"Captured flows & replay","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Tools"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/flows"},"158":{"id":"/docs/flows#0","page_id":"/docs/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/flows#format","content":"Format"},"159":{"id":"/docs/flows#1","page_id":"/docs/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/flows#the-index","content":"The index"},"160":{"id":"/docs/flows#2","page_id":"/docs/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/flows#replay","content":"Replay"},"161":{"id":"/docs/flows#3","page_id":"/docs/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/flows#why-this-beats-burp-here","content":"Why this beats Burp here"},"162":{"id":"/docs/flows#4","page_id":"/docs/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/flows#token-harvesting","content":"Token harvesting"},"163":{"id":"/docs/flows#5","page_id":"/docs/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/flows#spotting-the-interesting-things","content":"Spotting the interesting things"},"164":{"id":"/docs/flows#6","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows","content":"Every interesting request on the device ends up as a file in `/tmp/mtflows` (change with `FLOWDIR`). Those files are the raw material for everything else: analysis, replay, fuzzing, evidence."},"165":{"id":"/docs/flows#7","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#format","content":"One file per flow, named `<HHMMSS>_<host>_<path>.txt`:"},"166":{"id":"/docs/flows#8","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#format","content":"Notes:"},"167":{"id":"/docs/flows#9","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#format","content":"The headers block is mitmproxy's `Headers` repr on **one line** — parse with `ast.literal_eval` after stripping the `Headers` prefix (that is what `replay` does)."},"168":{"id":"/docs/flows#10","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#format","content":"Bodies are truncated at `MAXBODY` (20 000 bytes) but the index records the real lengths."},"169":{"id":"/docs/flows#11","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#format","content":"Two hosts with the same path no longer collide: the host is part of the name, and a `-2`/`-3` suffix is added if the same second produces the same host+path."},"170":{"id":"/docs/flows#12","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#format","content":"Names carry no date (only `HHMMSS`), so **never sort flows by name across days** — `session`, `replay` and `snap` sort by mtime."},"171":{"id":"/docs/flows#13","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#the-index","content":"Quick analysis:"},"172":{"id":"/docs/flows#14","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#replay","content":"`replay` re-issues a captured request from the host, defaulting to *exactly* what the app sent, with explicit overrides:"},"173":{"id":"/docs/flows#15","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#replay","content":"Patch syntax is a small JSONPath: `a.b`, `items[0].id`, `a.b[2].c`. Values are parsed as JSON when possible (`42`, `true`, `\"str\"`), else kept as strings."},"174":{"id":"/docs/flows#16","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#replay","content":"Every `--patch` run should start with `--dry`. It prints the method, URL, headers and the first 300 bytes of body — enough to catch a typo before you send something destructive to a production backend."},"175":{"id":"/docs/flows#17","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#why-this-beats-burp-here","content":"**Same headers** as the app, including device-specific ones and the cookie jar state at capture time."},"176":{"id":"/docs/flows#18","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#why-this-beats-burp-here","content":"**Attestation-friendly**: capture the login once, replay everything else; you never need a fresh keystore challenge for non-login endpoints."},"177":{"id":"/docs/flows#19","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#why-this-beats-burp-here","content":"**Evidence-friendly**: `-x` re-sends through mitmproxy, so the attempt lands in the same flow corpus with a timestamp."},"178":{"id":"/docs/flows#20","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#token-harvesting","content":"`session` merges the WebView's `document.cookie`, `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` with the newest captured `Cookie` header (httpOnly cookies are invisible to JS):"},"179":{"id":"/docs/flows#21","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#token-harvesting","content":"Storage layout:"},"180":{"id":"/docs/flows#22","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#spotting-the-interesting-things","content":"Patterns worth grepping for in a fresh corpus:"},"181":{"id":"/docs/flows#23","page_id":"/docs/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/flows#spotting-the-interesting-things","content":"And the classic: compare what a **low-privilege** account gets versus a **high-privilege** one for the same endpoint — same request, two cookies, diff the bodies."},"182":{"id":"/docs/frida","page_id":"/docs/frida","type":"page","content":"Frida & instrumentation","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","How it works"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/frida"},"183":{"id":"/docs/frida#0","page_id":"/docs/frida","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/frida#the-device-side","content":"The device side"},"184":{"id":"/docs/frida#1","page_id":"/docs/frida","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/frida#the-host-side","content":"The host side"},"185":{"id":"/docs/frida#2","page_id":"/docs/frida","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/frida#profiles","content":"Profiles"},"186":{"id":"/docs/frida#3","page_id":"/docs/frida","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/frida#the-local-script-set","content":"The local script set"},"187":{"id":"/docs/frida#4","page_id":"/docs/frida","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/frida#background-runs","content":"Background runs"},"188":{"id":"/docs/frida#5","page_id":"/docs/frida","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/frida#webview--cdp","content":"WebView = CDP"},"189":{"id":"/docs/frida#6","page_id":"/docs/frida","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/frida#stolen-modules-medusa","content":"Stolen modules (Medusa)"},"190":{"id":"/docs/frida#7","page_id":"/docs/frida","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/frida#when-frida-itself-is-the-problem","content":"When Frida itself is the problem"},"191":{"id":"/docs/frida#8","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida","content":"Frida is not \"installed\" here, it is **wired**: the agent autostarts as a Magisk module under a different name, listens on loopback only, and the host side is a set of script profiles that answer specific questions."},"192":{"id":"/docs/frida#9","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-device-side","content":"| Piece  | Path                                                             |\n| ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Binary | `/data/adb/fsrv/hluda` (renamed `frida-server`, 17.27.5, x86_64) |","table":"table-0"},"193":{"id":"/docs/frida#10","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-device-side","content":"| Piece  | Path                                                            |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Config | `/data/adb/fsrv/conf` → `AUTOSTART=1`, `LISTEN=127.0.0.1:27042` |","table":"table-0"},"194":{"id":"/docs/frida#11","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-device-side","content":"| Piece   | Path                                     |\n| ------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| Control | `/data/adb/fsrv/ctl start\\|stop\\|status` |","table":"table-0"},"195":{"id":"/docs/frida#12","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-device-side","content":"| Piece  | Path                                                   |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Module | `/data/adb/modules/fsrv` (starts it from `service.sh`) |","table":"table-0"},"196":{"id":"/docs/frida#13","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-device-side","content":"Renaming matters: the string `frida-server` and the default port `27042` are what most detectors grep for in `/proc/net/tcp`, process lists and file paths. `hluda` is what a heavily-used public build calls itself; on loopback it is also invisible to the LAN."},"197":{"id":"/docs/frida#14","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-host-side","content":"`frida` + `frida-tools` 17.27.5 (pipx), `objection` available for quick jobs, and these wrappers:"},"198":{"id":"/docs/frida#15","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#profiles","content":"| Profile | Scripts                             | Use it for                                               |\n| ------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `trace` | core, webview-debug, rootcheck, tls | first look: what does this app touch, what does it check |","table":"table-1"},"199":{"id":"/docs/frida#16","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#profiles","content":"| Profile | Scripts             | Use it for                               |\n| ------- | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `web`   | core, webview-debug | WebView/Tauri/Cordova apps — enables CDP |","table":"table-1"},"200":{"id":"/docs/frida#17","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#profiles","content":"| Profile  | Scripts        | Use it for                                        |\n| -------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `attest` | core, keystore | key generation, attestation challenge, chain dump |","table":"table-1"},"201":{"id":"/docs/frida#18","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#profiles","content":"| Profile | Scripts                                | Use it for                                       |\n| ------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `spy`   | core, webview-debug + 3 Medusa modules | anti-root bypass, OkHttp logging, SQLite queries |","table":"table-1"},"202":{"id":"/docs/frida#19","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#profiles","content":"| Profile     | Scripts                | Use it for                                                       |\n| ----------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `intercept` | 9 HTTP Toolkit scripts | pinning bypass + proxy override + CA injection + root-detect off |","table":"table-1"},"203":{"id":"/docs/frida#20","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#profiles","content":"| Profile | Scripts          | Use it for                 |\n| ------- | ---------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `full`  | everything local | kitchen sink; expect noise |","table":"table-1"},"204":{"id":"/docs/frida#21","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#profiles","content":"| Profile | Scripts | Use it for                              |\n| ------- | ------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `raw`   | none    | isolate whether a script is the problem |","table":"table-1"},"205":{"id":"/docs/frida#22","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-local-script-set","content":"| File         | What it hooks                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `00-core.js` | logging helpers on `globalThis`, process/arch info, a **filtered** exception handler (only reports faults in app-owned libs, capped at 5 — Frida 17 removed `global`; use `globalThis`) |","table":"table-2"},"206":{"id":"/docs/frida#23","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-local-script-set","content":"| File                  | What it hooks                                                               |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `05-webview-debug.js` | `WebView.setWebContentsDebuggingEnabled(true)`, console messages, URL loads |","table":"table-2"},"207":{"id":"/docs/frida#24","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-local-script-set","content":"| File        | What it hooks                                                                                                             |        |                |         |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------ | -------------- | ------- |\n| `10-jni.js` | scans loaded classes for `tauri`/`plugin` classes, wraps methods, lists `libapp_lib.so` symbols matching `permanent_login | attest | secure_storage | plugin` |","table":"table-2"},"208":{"id":"/docs/frida#25","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-local-script-set","content":"| File             | What it hooks                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `20-keystore.js` | `KeyGenParameterSpec.setAttestationChallenge` / `setIsStrongBoxBacked`, `KeyStore.getCertificateChain` subject/issuer dump |","table":"table-2"},"209":{"id":"/docs/frida#26","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-local-script-set","content":"| File              | What it hooks                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `30-rootcheck.js` | `File.exists/canRead/canExecute/isFile/isDirectory` on su/magisk/frida/xposed paths, `Runtime.exec`, `getPackageInfo`, `Debug.isDebuggerConnected`, `Build` fields |","table":"table-2"},"210":{"id":"/docs/frida#27","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#the-local-script-set","content":"| File        | What it hooks                                                                     |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `40-tls.js` | `SSLContext.init` trust managers, `NetworkSecurityPolicy`; `--bypass` = trust-all |","table":"table-2"},"211":{"id":"/docs/frida#28","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#background-runs","content":"Frida's REPL needs a tty. `frida -U -f pkg < /dev/null` exits immediately, and `pkill -f 'frida -U -f pkg'` can kill the shell that issued it. Use a fifo:"},"212":{"id":"/docs/frida#29","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#webview--cdp","content":"For hybrid apps this is the highest-value tool in the rig: no hooks, full DOM, console, network view and storage."},"213":{"id":"/docs/frida#30","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#webview--cdp","content":"`session` uses the same channel to merge `document.cookie`, `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` with the newest captured `cookie` header (httpOnly cookies never show up in JS)."},"214":{"id":"/docs/frida#31","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#stolen-modules-medusa","content":"`tools/medusa` is a vendored copy; `bin/medusa-export` converts its JSON modules into standalone JS:"},"215":{"id":"/docs/frida#32","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#stolen-modules-medusa","content":"Medusa's modules assume the framework's helpers (`colorLog`, `Module.findExportByName`). The exporter injects a shim: `Color`, `colorLog`, `Options` defaults, `__mod('libc.so', …)`, plus Frida-17 polyfills for `Module.findExportByName` / `getExportByName`."},"216":{"id":"/docs/frida#33","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#stolen-modules-medusa","content":"It replaces `getSharedPreferences()` globally and Chromium then dies with\n`NullPointerException: … SharedPreferences$Editor.apply() on a null object reference`.\nKeep it out of profiles for any app with a WebView; load it by hand only for native-only apps."},"217":{"id":"/docs/frida#34","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#when-frida-itself-is-the-problem","content":"| Symptom                                   | Cause                              | Fix                                       |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `Failed to spawn: unable to find process` | package not installed / wrong user | `adb shell pm list packages \\| grep name` |","table":"table-3"},"218":{"id":"/docs/frida#35","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#when-frida-itself-is-the-problem","content":"| Symptom                        | Cause                | Fix                                            |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| spawns then instantly detaches | script threw at load | run profile `raw`, then add scripts one by one |","table":"table-3"},"219":{"id":"/docs/frida#36","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#when-frida-itself-is-the-problem","content":"| Symptom                 | Cause                                              | Fix                                                             |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `access-violation` spam | the exception handler reporting ART's own SIGSEGVs | already filtered in `00-core.js`; check the PC is in an app lib |","table":"table-3"},"220":{"id":"/docs/frida#37","page_id":"/docs/frida","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/frida#when-frida-itself-is-the-problem","content":"| Symptom          | Cause                                      | Fix                        |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------ | -------------------------- |\n| `frida-ps` hangs | server died (OOM, or killed by a detector) | `/data/adb/fsrv/ctl start` |","table":"table-3"},"221":{"id":"/docs/glossary","page_id":"/docs/glossary","type":"page","content":"Glossary","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/glossary"},"222":{"id":"/docs/glossary#0","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**adb reverse** — forwards a port on the *device* to the host. Used so the app can reach mitmproxy on `127.0.0.1:18080` without a LAN proxy. Dies on every reboot."},"223":{"id":"/docs/glossary#1","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Attestation chain** — certificate chain returned by the Android keystore for a generated key: leaf (app key) → TEE intermediate → Droid CA → Google root. Encodes device identity, lock state and verified-boot status."},"224":{"id":"/docs/glossary#2","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**AVD** — Android Virtual Device. Here: `pentest16`, pixel_7 profile, API 36 Play Store image."},"225":{"id":"/docs/glossary#3","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Bootloader locked / verified boot** — properties the server can read from the attestation extension. TrickyStore's keybox decides what the server sees."},"226":{"id":"/docs/glossary#4","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**CDP** — Chrome DevTools Protocol. Over `adb forward :9222` it gives DOM, console, storage and network for any debuggable WebView."},"227":{"id":"/docs/glossary#5","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Cert-Fixer** — Magisk module that bind-mounts user CAs into `/apex/com.android.conscrypt/cacerts` at `post-fs-data`, so system apps (GMS, Play Store) trust mitmproxy."},"228":{"id":"/docs/glossary#6","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**conscrypt** — Android's TLS provider and the place the system trust store lives since Android 14 (moved out of `/system/etc/security/cacerts`)."},"229":{"id":"/docs/glossary#7","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**denylist (Magisk)** — packages that get *no* module injection. Empty in this rig on purpose: TrickyStore/PIF must reach the target app."},"230":{"id":"/docs/glossary#8","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**denylist policy (Zygisk Next)** — `default` (inject everywhere except denylisted) or `whitelist` (inject only listed). Whitelist breaks WebView renderer sandboxes."},"231":{"id":"/docs/glossary#9","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**frida-server** — the on-device agent. Here renamed `hluda`, autostarted by the `fsrv` Magisk module, listening on loopback only."},"232":{"id":"/docs/glossary#10","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**gadget** — Frida's injectable library for non-rooted devices; requires patching and re-signing the APK, which changes its signature. Not used here."},"233":{"id":"/docs/glossary#11","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**HMA-OSS** — \"Hide My Applist\" fork: hides installed packages from a target app's enumeration. Installed, hide list empty."},"234":{"id":"/docs/glossary#12","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**keybox.xml** — TrickyStore's replacement cert+key material: EC and/or RSA chains plus private keys. Must be hardware (RKP), unexpired and unrevoked."},"235":{"id":"/docs/glossary#13","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**keybox revocation list** — Google's published serial blacklist at `android.googleapis.com/attestation/status`. Server-side check; cannot be spoofed locally."},"236":{"id":"/docs/glossary#14","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**KVM** — kernel virtual machine; `/dev/kvm` + `kvm` group membership makes the emulator usable."},"237":{"id":"/docs/glossary#15","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Magisk** — systemless root. Version 31.1 here, applied to the system image's ramdisk via rootAVD."},"238":{"id":"/docs/glossary#16","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**mitmproxy / mitmdump** — the intercepting proxy. `mitm/dump.py` addon writes one file per flow."},"239":{"id":"/docs/glossary#17","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Play Integrity (PI)** — Google's app-level integrity API (device/app/account verdicts). Emulator → `NO_INTEGRITY`; not solvable here."},"240":{"id":"/docs/glossary#18","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**PIF (PlayIntegrityFix)** — module that tries to satisfy PI by spoofing props; on an emulator it still fails."},"241":{"id":"/docs/glossary#19","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**post-fs-data** — earliest Magisk boot stage; where Cert-Fixer mounts CAs."},"242":{"id":"/docs/glossary#20","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**RKP** — Remote Key Provisioning. Modern hardware attestation where keys/certs are provisioned by Google per device."},"243":{"id":"/docs/glossary#21","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**rootAVD** — script that patches an AVD's `ramdisk.img` with Magisk; modifies the system image, not the AVD config."},"244":{"id":"/docs/glossary#22","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**snapshot (AVD)** — full VM state save/restore (`adb emu avd snapshot save`). ~5 GB, ~25 s restore."},"245":{"id":"/docs/glossary#23","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**TrickyStore** — Zygisk module that substitutes keystore attestation chains for packages in `target.txt` using `keybox.xml`."},"246":{"id":"/docs/glossary#24","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**TEE** — Trusted Execution Environment; hardware side that produces attestation. Emulators fake it (`teeBroken=true`)."},"247":{"id":"/docs/glossary#25","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Zygisk** — Magisk's code-injection mechanism into zygote-spawned apps. Disabled in Magisk itself here; **Zygisk Next** provides it."},"248":{"id":"/docs/glossary#26","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**zygiskd** — Zygisk Next's control CLI (`status`, `enforce-denylist`, `denylist-policy`, `memory-type`)."},"249":{"id":"/docs/glossary#27","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**`Zygisk-Assistant`** — popular root-hiding module. Not used: it requires targets in Magisk's denylist, which strips our spoofing modules from those same apps."},"250":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"mobsec — an Android pentest rig that actually works","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"251":{"id":"/docs#0","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"What you get"},"252":{"id":"/docs#1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#30-second-health-check","content":"30-second health check"},"253":{"id":"/docs#2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#the-one-paragraph-mental-model","content":"The one-paragraph mental model"},"254":{"id":"/docs#3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#where-things-live","content":"Where things live"},"255":{"id":"/docs#4","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#start-reading-here","content":"Start reading here"},"256":{"id":"/docs#5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"A rooted Android 16 emulator on this laptop, wired end to end: **HTTPS decrypted**, **Frida attached from the first instruction**, **root hidden**, and **hardware-backed key attestation spoofed** well enough that a real bank-grade server accepts the login."},"257":{"id":"/docs#6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Everything here runs locally. No cloud, no extra hardware, ~20 GB of disk."},"258":{"id":"/docs#7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"The attestation layer makes this device claim to be a different physical phone, and the keybox in use is not ours. Use it against apps you are permitted to test. Nothing in this rig is anonymous: traffic goes out from your own IP."},"259":{"id":"/docs#8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                                   | How                                             | Page       |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| Android 16 x86_64 emulator, Play Store image | `pentest16` AVD (pixel_7, 6 GB RAM, 16 GB data) | Quickstart |","table":"table-0"},"260":{"id":"/docs#9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability            | How                                                                  | Page         |\n| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| Root + Magisk modules | rootAVD + Magisk 31.1, Zygisk Next, TrickyStore, PIF 4.9, Cert-Fixer | Architecture |","table":"table-0"},"261":{"id":"/docs#10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                         | How                                                 | Page         |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| HTTPS interception for *every* app | mitmproxy + system CA bind-mounted into `conscrypt` | Interception |","table":"table-0"},"262":{"id":"/docs#11","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                 | How                                              | Page         |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------ |\n| Certificate pinning bypass | HTTP Toolkit script set via `fspawn … intercept` | Interception |","table":"table-0"},"263":{"id":"/docs#12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                  | How                                                 | Page  |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ----- |\n| Frida, ready in one command | `frida-server` as a Magisk module + script profiles | Frida |","table":"table-0"},"264":{"id":"/docs#13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                           | How                                         | Page  |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- | ----- |\n| WebView DOM, console, storage access | Chrome DevTools Protocol over `adb forward` | Frida |","table":"table-0"},"265":{"id":"/docs#14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                          | How                         | Page  |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ----- |\n| Capture → edit → replay any request | `nettap` + `replay` harness | Flows |","table":"table-0"},"266":{"id":"/docs#15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                        | How                              | Page        |\n| --------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| Hardware key attestation spoofing | TrickyStore + a valid RKP keybox | Attestation |","table":"table-0"},"267":{"id":"/docs#16","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability           | How                                                                 | Page        |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| Root/emulator hiding | Zygisk denylist policy, anonymous memory, HMA-OSS scoped per target | Root hiding |","table":"table-0"},"268":{"id":"/docs#17","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                        | How                                       | Page           |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| Play Integrity verdicts, measured | `integrity` (drives SPIC, scrapes logcat) | Play Integrity |","table":"table-0"},"269":{"id":"/docs#18","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                                      | How                               | Page              |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| Exported components → ready-to-run adb commands | `entry` (manifest → attack sheet) | Command reference |","table":"table-0"},"270":{"id":"/docs#19","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                         | How                                           | Page              |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| App private storage off the device | `pull-data` (root tar + sqlite/prefs summary) | Command reference |","table":"table-0"},"271":{"id":"/docs#20","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                              | How                           | Page              |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| A checklist that maps to these commands | HackTricks/MASTG in rig terms | Pentest checklist |","table":"table-0"},"272":{"id":"/docs#21","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                      | How                                           | Page         |\n| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------ |\n| Static APK recon in one command | `recon` (apkid + apkleaks + mobsfscan + jadx) | Static recon |","table":"table-0"},"273":{"id":"/docs#22","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-get","content":"| Capability                          | How           | Page      |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------- | --------- |\n| Instant return to a logged-in state | AVD snapshots | Snapshots |","table":"table-0"},"274":{"id":"/docs#23","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#30-second-health-check","content":"If something is red, `pentestctl fix` repairs the two things that break on every reboot (`adb reverse` and the mitm addon), then see Troubleshooting."},"275":{"id":"/docs#24","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-one-paragraph-mental-model","content":"The emulator boots a **Magisk-patched ramdisk**, so `su` works from the first second. Magisk loads three Zygisk modules that matter: **TrickyStore** fakes the hardware keystore's attestation chain for packages listed in `target.txt`, **PlayIntegrityFix** tries (and fails, on an emulator) to satisfy Play Integrity, and **Zygisk Next** does the injecting in anonymous memory. **Cert-Fixer** bind-mounts our mitmproxy CA into every process's trust store, including system ones. **frida-server** runs renamed as `hluda` under a small custom module, listening on loopback only. On the host, `nettap` keeps mitmproxy and the `adb reverse` tunnel alive, `fspawn` starts an app under Frida with a chosen script profile, and `replay` re-issues anything you captured."},"276":{"id":"/docs#25","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#start-reading-here","content":"Quickstart — a device that is already built, or build it from zero."},"277":{"id":"/docs#26","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#start-reading-here","content":"Daily workflow — the loop you will actually repeat."},"278":{"id":"/docs#27","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#start-reading-here","content":"Architecture — why each layer exists, and what breaks without it."},"279":{"id":"/docs/integrity","page_id":"/docs/integrity","type":"page","content":"Play Integrity (the other attestation)","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","How it works"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrity"},"280":{"id":"/docs/integrity#0","page_id":"/docs/integrity","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrity#measuring-it-on-this-rig","content":"Measuring it on this rig"},"281":{"id":"/docs/integrity#1","page_id":"/docs/integrity","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrity#the-modules-and-why-they-do-not-help-here","content":"The modules, and why they do not help here"},"282":{"id":"/docs/integrity#2","page_id":"/docs/integrity","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrity#when-your-target-actually-gates-on-play-integrity","content":"When your target actually gates on Play Integrity"},"283":{"id":"/docs/integrity#3","page_id":"/docs/integrity","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrity#related-traps","content":"Related traps"},"284":{"id":"/docs/integrity#4","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity","content":"Two different things get called \"attestation\" in Android pentests, and confusing them wastes days:"},"285":{"id":"/docs/integrity#5","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity","content":"|                                              | What it proves                                              | Who checks it                      | Can this rig fake it?                           |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| **Key attestation** (Android Keystore / RKP) | \"this key lives in a TEE on a device whose boot state is X\" | your target's backend, per-request | **Yes** — TrickyStore + keybox, see Attestation |","table":"table-0"},"286":{"id":"/docs/integrity#6","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity","content":"|                                                               | What it proves                                                          | Who checks it                                         | Can this rig fake it?      |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| **Play Integrity** (`IntegrityManager.requestIntegrityToken`) | \"this APK, installed from Play, on a Google-approved device, right now\" | Google evaluates, your backend reads the verdict JSON | **No**, not on an emulator |","table":"table-0"},"287":{"id":"/docs/integrity#7","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity","content":"Play Integrity is Google's own server-side verdict. You cannot compute it locally, and the request only works for a Play-distributed, Play-signed app with a Play Console project — which is why pentest tooling ships its own checker APK."},"288":{"id":"/docs/integrity#8","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#measuring-it-on-this-rig","content":"`integrity` drives **SPIC** (`com.henrikherzig.playintegritychecker`, in `apks/`): force-stops it, launches it, finds the \"Make Play Integrity Request\" button via `uiautomator dump`, taps it, and parses the JSON block SPIC prints to `I/System.out` (that is where the library dumps the token payload)."},"289":{"id":"/docs/integrity#9","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#measuring-it-on-this-rig","content":"Measured on this AVD, twice, before and after PlayIntegrityFix:"},"290":{"id":"/docs/integrity#10","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#measuring-it-on-this-rig","content":"`UNEVALUATED` (and a *missing* `deviceRecognitionVerdict`) is not an error in the rig. Logcat shows the request itself succeeding:"},"291":{"id":"/docs/integrity#11","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#measuring-it-on-this-rig","content":"Google receives the request and declines to grade it: the device is an emulator and **no Google account is signed in**. Both conditions must be satisfied for a verdict to exist at all — and even with an account, a Play Store emulator image still cannot return `MEETS_DEVICE_INTEGRITY`."},"292":{"id":"/docs/integrity#12","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#measuring-it-on-this-rig","content":"It removes the `UNEVALUATED` state and replaces it with a clean `MEETS_BASIC_INTEGRITY` / no `DEVICE` result. It does not unlock anything, and it puts a real account on a rooted emulator."},"293":{"id":"/docs/integrity#13","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#the-modules-and-why-they-do-not-help-here","content":"**PlayIntegrityFix 4.9** (`playintegrityfix`) patches device props in GMS's process so DroidGuard is less likely to notice the emulator. It is installed and loading (`zygiskd status` lists it) — it just cannot manufacture a device verdict that Google refuses to issue."},"294":{"id":"/docs/integrity#14","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#the-modules-and-why-they-do-not-help-here","content":"**PlayIntegrityFork v19** is parked in `modules/archive/`: it ships **only** `arm64-v8a` and `armeabi-v7a` Zygisk libs, so on this x86_64 image it silently never loads. Watch for that class of bug with `zygiskd status` after every module change — the module staying absent from `modules64:` is the tell."},"295":{"id":"/docs/integrity#15","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#the-modules-and-why-they-do-not-help-here","content":"**TrickyStore** fakes the keystore chain. Play Integrity's `STRONG_INTEGRITY` needs a hardware-backed signature over the *app signing key* by a Google-trusted root — key attestation spoofing gets you partway, then Google's own evaluation of the resulting record is the wall."},"296":{"id":"/docs/integrity#16","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#the-modules-and-why-they-do-not-help-here","content":"**TEESimulator** (JingMatrix, GPL-3.0) is the current community answer: a software KeyMint that needs a keybox, designed for exactly this \"make a non-device look like a device\" problem. It is a candidate upgrade for this rig; it is not installed, and it would still be fighting Play's verdict rather than key attestation."},"297":{"id":"/docs/integrity#17","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#when-your-target-actually-gates-on-play-integrity","content":"In order of cost:"},"298":{"id":"/docs/integrity#18","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#when-your-target-actually-gates-on-play-integrity","content":"**Check it is really PI.** If the app also sends a key-attestation chain (Tauri/Rust/native apps often do), the keybox path already covers you — Target is exactly this case."},"299":{"id":"/docs/integrity#19","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#when-your-target-actually-gates-on-play-integrity","content":"**Frida-hook the client side.** `IntegrityManager.requestIntegrityToken` / the verdict parser in the app: hook the callback and hand back a verdict the app likes. Works only when the backend trusts the *client* to inspect the verdict, which is a bug worth reporting in itself."},"300":{"id":"/docs/integrity#20","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#when-your-target-actually-gates-on-play-integrity","content":"**Replay with a good token.** `session` + `replay` let you re-issue the request with a token minted on a clean device — that is the same thing a real attacker does, and it demonstrates the missing server-side binding."},"301":{"id":"/docs/integrity#21","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#when-your-target-actually-gates-on-play-integrity","content":"**Use a physical device.** No emulator configuration passes `MEETS_DEVICE_INTEGRITY`; that is the point of the product."},"302":{"id":"/docs/integrity#22","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#related-traps","content":"`uiautomator dump` returns nothing useful on a locked screen, and the tap lands nowhere. `adb shell input keyevent KEYCODE_WAKEUP` first if the AVD has been idle."},"303":{"id":"/docs/integrity#23","page_id":"/docs/integrity","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrity#related-traps","content":"The verdict is a multi-line pretty-printed document in logcat. Closing braces of nested objects are indented; only the final one is flush left. Any scraper that stops at the first `}` truncates the JSON and reports \"no verdict\" — a bug that cost an hour here."},"304":{"id":"/docs/interception","page_id":"/docs/interception","type":"page","content":"HTTPS interception","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","How it works"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/interception"},"305":{"id":"/docs/interception#0","page_id":"/docs/interception","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/interception#the-chain","content":"The chain"},"306":{"id":"/docs/interception#1","page_id":"/docs/interception","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/interception#the-ca-exactly","content":"The CA, exactly"},"307":{"id":"/docs/interception#2","page_id":"/docs/interception","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/interception#pinning","content":"Pinning"},"308":{"id":"/docs/interception#3","page_id":"/docs/interception","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/interception#what-still-resists","content":"What still resists"},"309":{"id":"/docs/interception#4","page_id":"/docs/interception","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/interception#the-addon","content":"The addon"},"310":{"id":"/docs/interception#5","page_id":"/docs/interception","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/interception#sanity-checks-that-catch-most-interception-is-broken-reports","content":"Sanity checks that catch most \"interception is broken\" reports"},"311":{"id":"/docs/interception#6","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception","content":"The goal is boring reliability: every app on the device, including Play Store and GMS, decrypts through mitmproxy, and apps that pin certificates still connect."},"312":{"id":"/docs/interception#7","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-chain","content":"<Mermaid chart=\"flowchart LR A[app] -->|CONNECT :18080| B[adb reverse tunnel] B --> C[mitmdump :18080<br/>mitm/dump.…\" />"},"313":{"id":"/docs/interception#8","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-chain","content":"**`adb reverse tcp:18080 tcp:18080`** — device port 18080 is the host's mitmdump. Survives nothing; re-established by `nettap on`."},"314":{"id":"/docs/interception#9","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-chain","content":"**Global proxy** `127.0.0.1:18080` (optional once `fspawn intercept` is in play)."},"315":{"id":"/docs/interception#10","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-chain","content":"**CA trust** — the mitmproxy CA is installed as a *user* CA (`/data/misc/user/0/cacerts-added/<hash>.0`) and then mounted into the system trust store by **Cert-Fixer** at boot."},"316":{"id":"/docs/interception#11","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-chain","content":"**Capture** — `mitm/dump.py` writes one file per interesting flow."},"317":{"id":"/docs/interception#12","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-ca-exactly","content":"Installed at `/data/misc/user/0/cacerts-added/c8750f0d.0`; Cert-Fixer copies and bind-mounts it into `/apex/com.android.conscrypt/cacerts` for every process, and does the same inside PID 1's mount namespace so late-started system services inherit it."},"318":{"id":"/docs/interception#13","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-ca-exactly","content":"Verify for a specific process:"},"319":{"id":"/docs/interception#14","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-ca-exactly","content":"That module only mounts in `service.sh`, i.e. **after** GMS and Play Store have already started, so they kept their original trust store and failed with `Client TLS handshake failed … does not trust the proxy's certificate for play-fe.googleapis.com`. Cert-Fixer hooks `post-fs-data` instead. It is installed, `trustusercerts` is disabled via `touch /data/adb/modules/trustusercerts/disable`."},"320":{"id":"/docs/interception#15","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#pinning","content":"Two independent mechanisms, both from HTTP Toolkit's Frida scripts (`frida/httptoolkit/`), loaded by `fspawn <pkg> intercept`:"},"321":{"id":"/docs/interception#16","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#pinning","content":"**`android-certificate-unpinning.js`** — hooks `TrustManagerImpl`, `OkHttp CertificatePinner`, `X509TrustManager` wrappers, Conscrypt and a long list of third-party pinning libraries, and makes them accept anything."},"322":{"id":"/docs/interception#17","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#pinning","content":"**`android-certificate-unpinning-fallback.js`** — a second pass that patches classes *after* they load, for apps that cache their trust managers early."},"323":{"id":"/docs/interception#18","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#pinning","content":"Plus two scripts that make interception work without a system proxy:"},"324":{"id":"/docs/interception#19","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#pinning","content":"**`android-proxy-override.js`** — rewrites `System.getProperty(\"http.proxyHost\")`, `ConnectivityManager.getDefaultProxy()` and OkHttp's proxy selector."},"325":{"id":"/docs/interception#20","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#pinning","content":"**`native-connect-hook.js` / `native-tls-hook.js`** — LD_PRELOAD-style hooks (`connect`, `getaddrinfo`, `SSL_*`) so native code (Rust/Flutter/Go) also goes through the proxy and trusts our CA."},"326":{"id":"/docs/interception#21","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#pinning","content":"Proof, reproducible on this device:"},"327":{"id":"/docs/interception#22","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#pinning","content":"Without the profile the same button says **Failed** and no flow appears."},"328":{"id":"/docs/interception#23","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#what-still-resists","content":"| Case                                     | Symptom                                                             | Workaround                                                                                      |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Certificate **transparency** enforcement | `SSL handshake failed` inside a pinned library, even with unpinning | Not solved here; needs a CT-aware proxy or hooking the CT verifier (`--ct` hooks in some forks) |","table":"table-0"},"329":{"id":"/docs/interception#24","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#what-still-resists","content":"| Case                           | Symptom                      | Workaround                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Mutual TLS with a hardware key | login fails at the TLS layer | Keys live in TEE; only TrickyStore-style keystore spoofing can help, and only for attestation, not arbitrary mTLS |","table":"table-0"},"330":{"id":"/docs/interception#25","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#what-still-resists","content":"| Case          | Symptom                     | Workaround                                                                            |\n| ------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| QUIC / HTTP/3 | app works, nothing captured | Disable QUIC in the app or block UDP 443 on the device; mitmproxy does not proxy QUIC |","table":"table-0"},"331":{"id":"/docs/interception#26","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#what-still-resists","content":"| Case                 | Symptom                 | Workaround                                                                                  |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| WebSocket over `wss` | decrypted once upgraded | mitmproxy captures the upgrade; use the addon's `websocket_message` hook if you need frames |","table":"table-0"},"332":{"id":"/docs/interception#27","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#what-still-resists","content":"| Case                                                  | Symptom                     | Workaround                                                                                     |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Apps that pin inside a **WebView WebAssembly** module | nothing in Java hooks fires | hook the WebView's network stack (`fspawn web`) or fall back to `replay` with harvested tokens |","table":"table-0"},"333":{"id":"/docs/interception#28","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-addon","content":"`FLOWDIR` (default `/tmp/mtflows`), `INTEREST` (only matching URLs), `IGNORE` (default drops googleapis/gstatic/ggbn/firebase/app-measurement/crashlytics noise), `MAXBODY` (20000 bytes per body)."},"334":{"id":"/docs/interception#29","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-addon","content":"Output `<HHMMSS>_<host>_<path>.txt`, plus `_index.log` (human) and `_index.jsonl` (machine)."},"335":{"id":"/docs/interception#30","page_id":"/docs/interception","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interception#the-addon","content":"Restart after editing: `nettap off && nettap on`. mitmproxy does **not** hot-reload addons."},"336":{"id":"/docs/quickstart","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","type":"page","content":"Quickstart","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/quickstart"},"337":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#0","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/quickstart#path-a--the-device-already-exists","content":"Path A — the device already exists"},"338":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#1","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/quickstart#path-b--rebuild-from-zero","content":"Path B — rebuild from zero"},"339":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#2","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/quickstart#first-real-verification-5-minutes","content":"First real verification (5 minutes)"},"340":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#3","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/quickstart#sharing-this-site","content":"Sharing this site"},"341":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#4","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/quickstart#where-to-go-next","content":"Where to go next"},"342":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#5","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart","content":"Two paths: the device already exists (this laptop), or you are rebuilding it on a fresh machine."},"343":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#6","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#path-a--the-device-already-exists","content":"`snap load` restores apps, sessions and cookies exactly as you left them. See Snapshots."},"344":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#7","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#path-b--rebuild-from-zero","content":"The full beginner walkthrough (SDK install, AVD tuning, rootAVD/Magisk UI clicks, module URLs, CA install, verification) lives in `GUIDE-from-scratch.md` in the repo root (open it directly, it is not part of this site). Short version:"},"345":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#8","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#path-b--rebuild-from-zero","content":"Order matters: `install-device.sh` reboots the device, `setup-net.sh` must run **after** the first boot with modules installed, and `setup-keybox.sh` last (it validates against the live device's TrickyStore path)."},"346":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#9","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#path-b--rebuild-from-zero","content":"Magisk's \"install → patch image → additional setup → reboot\" flow is UI-driven. `rootAVD.sh` pauses for it; the `GUIDE-from-scratch.md` section 4 walks the exact taps, and `uitap` can drive most of them by text."},"347":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#10","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#first-real-verification-5-minutes","content":"Do not trust a green `pentestctl status` alone — prove each layer with a request:"},"348":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#11","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#first-real-verification-5-minutes","content":"| Layer        | Command                                                                         | Expected                    |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Interception | `curl -s -x 127.0.0.1:18080 -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' https://example.org` | `200`, plus a new flow file |","table":"table-0"},"349":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#12","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#first-real-verification-5-minutes","content":"| Layer              | Command                                | Expected                                    |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| System trust (GMS) | open Play Store, check `/tmp/mitm.log` | no `does not trust the proxy's certificate` |","table":"table-0"},"350":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#13","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#first-real-verification-5-minutes","content":"| Layer          | Command                                                                        | Expected                                         |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| Pinning bypass | `fspawn tech.httptoolkit.pinning_demo intercept` → tap \"OkHTTP pinned request\" | label says **Success**, request appears in flows |","table":"table-0"},"351":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#14","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#first-real-verification-5-minutes","content":"| Layer | Command                           | Expected                                  |\n| ----- | --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Frida | `fspawn com.android.settings web` | `[fspawn] … scripts=2`, no exception spam |","table":"table-0"},"352":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#15","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#first-real-verification-5-minutes","content":"| Layer       | Command          | Expected           |\n| ----------- | ---------------- | ------------------ |\n| WebView CDP | `fdp && cdp url` | the app's page URL |","table":"table-0"},"353":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#16","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#first-real-verification-5-minutes","content":"| Layer       | Command                             | Expected                                                  |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Attestation | `KeyAttestation` app → \"Attest key\" | leaf issuer `O=TEE,CN=<deviceid>`, \"Bootloader is locked\" |","table":"table-0"},"354":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#17","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#sharing-this-site","content":"The site is served by MkDocs on the host. By default it listens on loopback only:"},"355":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#18","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#sharing-this-site","content":"Two things have to be true for another device to load it:"},"356":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#19","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#sharing-this-site","content":"**It is bound to `0.0.0.0`**, not `127.0.0.1` (`docs serve --lan` does that; `docs status` shows the bind)."},"357":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#20","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#sharing-this-site","content":"**The host firewall lets the port in.** On a box with `ufw` enabled the default inbound policy is\n`DROP`, so once:"},"358":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#21","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#sharing-this-site","content":"To keep it up permanently (survives logout/reboot, restarts on failure):"},"359":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#22","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#sharing-this-site","content":"It is a plain MkDocs site: no auth, no TLS. Anyone on that network can read the whole rig, including\nwhich target you are testing — put it behind Tailscale or an SSH tunnel\n(`ssh -L 8000:127.0.0.1:8000 host`) if the network is not yours."},"360":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#23","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#where-to-go-next","content":"Daily workflow — the loop on a real engagement."},"361":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#24","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#where-to-go-next","content":"Interception — why pinning bypass works, and what still fails."},"362":{"id":"/docs/quickstart#25","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#where-to-go-next","content":"Troubleshooting — the eight traps, in the order they usually hit."},"363":{"id":"/docs/rebuild","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","type":"page","content":"Rebuild from scratch","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/rebuild"},"364":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#0","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rebuild#automated-path","content":"Automated path"},"365":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#1","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rebuild#why-the-order-is-fixed","content":"Why the order is fixed"},"366":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#2","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rebuild#what-is-interactive","content":"What is interactive"},"367":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#3","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rebuild#sharing-the-rig-with-a-colleague","content":"Sharing the rig with a colleague"},"368":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#4","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rebuild#verification-after-a-rebuild","content":"Verification after a rebuild"},"369":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#5","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rebuild#version-pinning-that-matters","content":"Version pinning that matters"},"370":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#6","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild","content":"Two artefacts describe a rebuild:"},"371":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#7","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild","content":"**`GUIDE-from-scratch.md`** — the narrative walkthrough (12 sections, beginner-friendly, includes the interactive Magisk UI steps and every download URL)."},"372":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#8","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild","content":"**`bootstrap.sh` / `fetch-deps.sh` / `install-device.sh` / `setup-keybox.sh` / `setup-net.sh`** — the automated path, in that order."},"373":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#9","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#why-the-order-is-fixed","content":"| Step           | Depends on | Fails if skipped        |\n| -------------- | ---------- | ----------------------- |\n| `bootstrap.sh` | —          | no SDK/adb/emulator/AVD |","table":"table-0"},"374":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#10","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#why-the-order-is-fixed","content":"| Step            | Depends on | Fails if skipped              |\n| --------------- | ---------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `fetch-deps.sh` | network    | nothing to install downstream |","table":"table-0"},"375":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#11","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#why-the-order-is-fixed","content":"| Step    | Depends on              | Fails if skipped                           |\n| ------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| rootAVD | booted, unrooted device | `install-device.sh` aborts on missing `su` |","table":"table-0"},"376":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#12","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#why-the-order-is-fixed","content":"| Step                | Depends on | Fails if skipped                   |\n| ------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `install-device.sh` | root       | no TrickyStore/PIF/Cert-Fixer/fsrv |","table":"table-0"},"377":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#13","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#why-the-order-is-fixed","content":"| Step              | Depends on            | Fails if skipped                |\n| ----------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `setup-keybox.sh` | TrickyStore on device | attestation stays software/AOSP |","table":"table-0"},"378":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#14","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#why-the-order-is-fixed","content":"| Step           | Depends on                      | Fails if skipped                      |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `setup-net.sh` | Cert-Fixer installed + one boot | user apps work, GMS/Play Store do not |","table":"table-0"},"379":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#15","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#why-the-order-is-fixed","content":"`install-device.sh` finishes with a reboot; wait for `adb wait-for-device` before continuing."},"380":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#16","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#what-is-interactive","content":"Only Magisk's first-run flow: *Install → Patch firmware/image → Select from storage → fakeboot.img → OK → additional setup → reboot*, plus granting `su` to shell. `GUIDE §4` has the exact taps; `uitap` can drive them by text, but expect to babysit it once."},"381":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#17","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#sharing-the-rig-with-a-colleague","content":"Deliberately excluded, with reasons:"},"382":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#18","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#sharing-the-rig-with-a-colleague","content":"| Excluded                     | Why                                              |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `keybox.xml`, `.pem`, `.p12` | key material; the recipient must fetch their own |","table":"table-1"},"383":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#19","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#sharing-the-rig-with-a-colleague","content":"| Excluded                            | Why                                     |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `~/.mobsec/session`, `~/.mitmproxy` | live cookies/tokens and your private CA |","table":"table-1"},"384":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#20","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#sharing-the-rig-with-a-colleague","content":"| Excluded      | Why                      |\n| ------------- | ------------------------ |\n| AVD snapshots | 5 GB each, host-specific |","table":"table-1"},"385":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#21","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#sharing-the-rig-with-a-colleague","content":"| Excluded                                   | Why                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| tool binaries (jadx, scrcpy, frida-server) | re-downloadable via `fetch-deps.sh`, keeps the zip ~25 MB |","table":"table-1"},"386":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#22","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#sharing-the-rig-with-a-colleague","content":"| Excluded            | Why                                     |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `MagiskFrida-*.zip` | 141 MB, superseded by the `fsrv` module |","table":"table-1"},"387":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#23","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#sharing-the-rig-with-a-colleague","content":"The recipient still needs **their own** `adb` device and must run `setup-net.sh` so their mitmproxy CA (not ours) is installed. `SHARING.md` in the archive carries the exact run order and this table."},"388":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#24","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#version-pinning-that-matters","content":"| Component | Version | Why pinned                                                            |\n| --------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Magisk    | 31.1    | Zygisk Next expects it; older Magisk has no `--sqlite` settings write |","table":"table-2"},"389":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#25","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#version-pinning-that-matters","content":"| Component   | Version   | Why pinned                           |\n| ----------- | --------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Zygisk Next | 1.5.3-880 | later builds changed `zygiskd` flags |","table":"table-2"},"390":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#26","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#version-pinning-that-matters","content":"| Component    | Version | Why pinned                                                                   |\n| ------------ | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| frida-server | 17.27.5 | must match host `frida` exactly; 17.x removed `global`, changed `Module` API |","table":"table-2"},"391":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#27","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#version-pinning-that-matters","content":"| Component  | Version | Why pinned                                                  |\n| ---------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Frida host | 17.27.5 | mismatch = \"unable to communicate with remote frida-server\" |","table":"table-2"},"392":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#28","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#version-pinning-that-matters","content":"| Component        | Version      | Why pinned                   |\n| ---------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------- |\n| PlayIntegrityFix | 4.9-inject-s | v19 has no x86_64 zygisk lib |","table":"table-2"},"393":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#29","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#version-pinning-that-matters","content":"| Component | Version | Why pinned                |\n| --------- | ------- | ------------------------- |\n| jadx      | 1.5.7   | apkleaks shells out to it |","table":"table-2"},"394":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#30","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#version-pinning-that-matters","content":"| Component | Version | Why pinned                                      |\n| --------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| mitmproxy | 12.3.1  | addon uses `http.HTTPFlow` API (stable since 9) |","table":"table-2"},"395":{"id":"/docs/rebuild#31","page_id":"/docs/rebuild","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rebuild#version-pinning-that-matters","content":"When you bump a version, re-run the verification list top to bottom before trusting the rig."},"396":{"id":"/docs/recon","page_id":"/docs/recon","type":"page","content":"Static recon","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Tools"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/recon"},"397":{"id":"/docs/recon#0","page_id":"/docs/recon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/recon#usage","content":"Usage"},"398":{"id":"/docs/recon#1","page_id":"/docs/recon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/recon#what-the-report-contains-and-how-to-read-it","content":"What the report contains, and how to read it"},"399":{"id":"/docs/recon#2","page_id":"/docs/recon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/recon#exported-components","content":"Exported components"},"400":{"id":"/docs/recon#3","page_id":"/docs/recon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"Packers / anti-analysis (APKiD)"},"401":{"id":"/docs/recon#4","page_id":"/docs/recon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/recon#secrets--endpoints-apkleaks","content":"Secrets / endpoints (apkleaks)"},"402":{"id":"/docs/recon#5","page_id":"/docs/recon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/recon#sast-mobsfscan","content":"SAST (mobsfscan)"},"403":{"id":"/docs/recon#6","page_id":"/docs/recon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/recon#deep-mode","content":"Deep mode"},"404":{"id":"/docs/recon#7","page_id":"/docs/recon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/recon#a-realistic-order-of-operations","content":"A realistic order of operations"},"405":{"id":"/docs/recon#8","page_id":"/docs/recon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/recon#extending-it","content":"Extending it"},"406":{"id":"/docs/recon#9","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon","content":"Dynamic testing tells you what the app *did*; static testing tells you what it *can* do. `recon` runs the static pass in one command and produces a report you can read in two minutes."},"407":{"id":"/docs/recon#10","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#usage","content":"Output:"},"408":{"id":"/docs/recon#11","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#exported-components","content":"The attack surface that does not require the app to be running. For each component: `permission`, `actions`, `categories`, `data` (scheme/host/path/mime). Anything exported without a signature-level permission is worth a `adb shell am start` / `am broadcast` probe."},"409":{"id":"/docs/recon#12","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"Read this with suspicion. APKiD matches library code too:"},"410":{"id":"/docs/recon#13","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"| Tag         | Meaning                     | What to do                                            |\n| ----------- | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `packer: …` | packer/obfuscator heuristic | decide whether to test the packed layer or the loader |","table":"table-0"},"411":{"id":"/docs/recon#14","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"| Tag                      | Meaning                  | What to do                                          |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `anti_vm` / `anti_debug` | emulator/debugger checks | **verify by reading the class** before believing it |","table":"table-0"},"412":{"id":"/docs/recon#15","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"| Tag                 | Meaning            | What to do |\n| ------------------- | ------------------ | ---------- |\n| `compiler: unknown` | not a real finding | ignore     |","table":"table-0"},"413":{"id":"/docs/recon#16","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"Concrete example from this rig: Target was tagged `anti_vm` + `packer: DexGuard`, and every hit turned out to be library code:"},"414":{"id":"/docs/recon#17","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"`W0/c.java` → Firebase CCT metadata (`sdk-version`, `Build.MODEL`, `Build.FINGERPRINT`)"},"415":{"id":"/docs/recon#18","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"`p003a2/v.java` → Material `MaterialAutoCompleteTextView` (a Meizu hint workaround)"},"416":{"id":"/docs/recon#19","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"`p045n1/k.java` → GMS `DialogRedirect` logging"},"417":{"id":"/docs/recon#20","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"`p019g/A.java` → `!\"robolectric\".equals(Build.FINGERPRINT)`"},"418":{"id":"/docs/recon#21","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#packers--anti-analysis-apkid","content":"So: no app-level emulator check in the DEX. The `DexGuard` tag was R8 single-letter-package confusion. Ten minutes of reading beat a day of chasing a phantom."},"419":{"id":"/docs/recon#22","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#secrets--endpoints-apkleaks","content":"Categories with hit counts. Triage rules:"},"420":{"id":"/docs/recon#23","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#secrets--endpoints-apkleaks","content":"`Google_API_Key` / `Firebase` keys are **usually not secrets** — they are restricted by package name + SHA-1. Report only if a restriction test shows otherwise."},"421":{"id":"/docs/recon#24","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#secrets--endpoints-apkleaks","content":"Random 30–40 char strings tagged `Artifactory_Password` are frequently obfuscation noise; grep the decompiled tree for the value before writing a finding."},"422":{"id":"/docs/recon#25","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#secrets--endpoints-apkleaks","content":"Version strings (`1.0.0.2`) match `IP_Address`; ignore."},"423":{"id":"/docs/recon#26","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#secrets--endpoints-apkleaks","content":"Real finds look like: hardcoded bearer tokens, private endpoints, staging hosts, cloud storage buckets."},"424":{"id":"/docs/recon#27","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#sast-mobsfscan","content":"Rule-based Android checks (exported components, weak crypto, WebView settings, backup flags…). Fast, noisy, useful as a checklist. Zero findings is a valid result — not proof of safety."},"425":{"id":"/docs/recon#28","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#deep-mode","content":"`--deep` decompiles with jadx (1.5.7) and greps string literals for URLs, then writes `endpoints.txt`. Use it to build the API list before you even launch the app; combine with the captured flows later."},"426":{"id":"/docs/recon#29","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#a-realistic-order-of-operations","content":"`recon com.example.app --deep` — components, permissions, endpoints, secrets."},"427":{"id":"/docs/recon#30","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#a-realistic-order-of-operations","content":"Note the **exported** components and any endpoint that looks internal (`/admin`, `/internal`, versioned staging hosts)."},"428":{"id":"/docs/recon#31","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#a-realistic-order-of-operations","content":"Launch with `fspawn com.example.app web` (or `intercept`) and capture the real request set."},"429":{"id":"/docs/recon#32","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#a-realistic-order-of-operations","content":"Diff static endpoints vs captured endpoints: what the app *can* call but did not is where the interesting bugs live."},"430":{"id":"/docs/recon#33","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#a-realistic-order-of-operations","content":"Only then start `replay` fuzzing."},"431":{"id":"/docs/recon#34","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#extending-it","content":"`recon` is a shell script; every step is independent (`aapt2`, `apkanalyzer`, `apkid`, `apkleaks`, `mobsfscan`, `jadx`). Add steps by copying the pattern in `~/mobsec/bin/recon` — each writes into `raw/` and appends a section to `report.md`."},"432":{"id":"/docs/recon#35","page_id":"/docs/recon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/recon#extending-it","content":"Useful manual follow-ups it does not do:"},"433":{"id":"/docs/snapshots","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","type":"page","content":"Snapshots","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Tools"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/snapshots"},"434":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#0","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/snapshots#commands","content":"Commands"},"435":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#1","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/snapshots#what-survives-a-restore","content":"What survives a restore"},"436":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#2","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/snapshots#when-a-snapshot-is-a-trap","content":"When a snapshot is a trap"},"437":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#3","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/snapshots#cost","content":"Cost"},"438":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#4","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots","content":"A cold boot costs ~90 seconds plus a login. A snapshot restore costs ~25 seconds and comes back to whatever state was saved — **including a logged-in app, if that is what you froze**."},"439":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#5","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#commands","content":"Under the hood:"},"440":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#6","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#commands","content":"`-no-snapshot-save` is deliberate: when the emulator exits it would otherwise overwrite the snapshot with whatever half-broken state you were in."},"441":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#7","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#what-survives-a-restore","content":"| Survives                      | Does not survive                 |\n| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| installed apps and their data | `adb reverse` tunnel (host-side) |","table":"table-0"},"442":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#8","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#what-survives-a-restore","content":"| Survives                                  | Does not survive             |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| logged-in sessions/cookies in app storage | mitmdump process (host-side) |","table":"table-0"},"443":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#9","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#what-survives-a-restore","content":"| Survives                     | Does not survive                                      |\n| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Magisk modules + mount state | sometimes frida-server (`pentestctl fix` restarts it) |","table":"table-0"},"444":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#10","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#what-survives-a-restore","content":"| Survives           | Does not survive                                              |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| keybox, target.txt | global proxy setting? (survives, but points at a dead tunnel) |","table":"table-0"},"445":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#11","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#what-survives-a-restore","content":"That is why the documented restore sequence is:"},"446":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#12","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#when-a-snapshot-is-a-trap","content":"Snapshots capture **mount state**, so a snapshot taken while a module was broken keeps restoring the broken mount. Symptoms: Cert-Fixer log says it ran, but GMS still cannot TLS. Fix: cold boot (`snap boot`), verify, then `snap save` again under a new name."},"447":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#13","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#when-a-snapshot-is-a-trap","content":"Rules:"},"448":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#14","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#when-a-snapshot-is-a-trap","content":"After installing/removing a Magisk module or changing the CA, **cold boot once**, verify `pentestctl status` + a GMS request, then save a new snapshot."},"449":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#15","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#when-a-snapshot-is-a-trap","content":"Keep at most a handful: each is ~5 GB."},"450":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#16","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#when-a-snapshot-is-a-trap","content":"Name by intent (`logged-in`, `pre-fuzz`, `clean-no-modules`), not by date."},"451":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#17","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#when-a-snapshot-is-a-trap","content":"**A snapshot is only as logged-in as the moment you saved it.** After `keybox-refresh` rotates the\nkeybox, the device presents a new attestation identity on the next launch and the backend drops the\nsession — a snapshot saved before the rotation restores a logged-out app. Re-login (you need the\nTOTP), then `snap save logged-in` again."},"452":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#18","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#when-a-snapshot-is-a-trap","content":"`load`/`boot` start the emulator with `-no-snapshot-save` so a broken session cannot overwrite a\ngood snapshot. The emulator reports the refusal as `UNSUPPORTED_VK_APP`, which looks like a GPU\nproblem and is not. `snap save <name> --reopen` cold-boots keeping `/data`, then saves."},"453":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#19","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#cost","content":"| Action    | Time  | Disk |\n| --------- | ----- | ---- |\n| cold boot | ~90 s | —    |","table":"table-1"},"454":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#20","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#cost","content":"| Action           | Time     | Disk |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ---- |\n| snapshot restore | ~21–25 s | —    |","table":"table-1"},"455":{"id":"/docs/snapshots#21","page_id":"/docs/snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/snapshots#cost","content":"| Action       | Time | Disk    |\n| ------------ | ---- | ------- |\n| one snapshot | —    | ~5.2 GB |","table":"table-1"},"456":{"id":"/docs/status","page_id":"/docs/status","type":"page","content":"Live status","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/status"},"457":{"id":"/docs/status#0","page_id":"/docs/status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/status#platform","content":"Platform"},"458":{"id":"/docs/statu