---------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Key attestation spoofing | <StatusBadge variant=\"ok\">working</StatusBadge> | server accepted login with a 5-cert RKP chain |","table":"table-3"},"488":{"id":"/docs/status#31","page_id":"/docs/status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/status#coverage-at-a-glance","content":"| Capability                         | State          | Note                            |\n| ---------------------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| Root hiding (paths, memory, ports) | <StatusBadge variant=\"ok\">working</StatusBadge> | anonymous memory, renamed agent |","table":"table-3"},"489":{"id":"/docs/status#32","page_id":"/docs/status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/status#coverage-at-a-glance","content":"| Capability                    | State                 | Note            |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------- | --------------- |\n| Package-list hiding (HMA-OSS) | <StatusBadge variant=\"warn\">not configured</StatusBadge> | hide list empty |","table":"table-3"},"490":{"id":"/docs/status#33","page_id":"/docs/status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/status#coverage-at-a-glance","content":"| Capability                    | State                    | Note                                         |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| Play Integrity device verdict | <StatusBadge variant=\"bad\">not possible here</StatusBadge> | emulator limitation; needs a physical device |","table":"table-3"},"491":{"id":"/docs/status#34","page_id":"/docs/status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/status#coverage-at-a-glance","content":"| Capability                           | State              | Note      |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------ | --------- |\n| Certificate transparency-pinned apps | <StatusBadge variant=\"bad\">unsupported</StatusBadge> | known gap |","table":"table-3"},"492":{"id":"/docs/status#35","page_id":"/docs/status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/status#known-good-invariants","content":"If any of those drift, run `pentestctl fix` and read Troubleshooting."},"493":{"id":"/docs/stealth","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"page","content":"Root hiding","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","How it works"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth"},"494":{"id":"/docs/stealth#0","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth#what-is-hidden-and-how","content":"What is hidden, and how"},"495":{"id":"/docs/stealth#1","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth#zygisk-next-knobs","content":"Zygisk Next knobs"},"496":{"id":"/docs/stealth#2","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth#the-whitelist-trap","content":"The whitelist trap"},"497":{"id":"/docs/stealth#3","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth#magisk-denylist-keep-it-empty","content":"Magisk denylist: keep it empty"},"498":{"id":"/docs/stealth#4","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth#traps","content":"Traps"},"499":{"id":"/docs/stealth#5","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth#hma-oss-hiding-packages-from-one-app-at-a-time","content":"HMA-OSS: hiding packages from one app at a time"},"500":{"id":"/docs/stealth#6","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth#the-file-that-matters","content":"The file that matters"},"501":{"id":"/docs/stealth#7","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth#doing-it-from-the-host-not-the-ui","content":"Doing it from the host, not the UI"},"502":{"id":"/docs/stealth#8","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth#verifying-hiding-actually-works","content":"Verifying hiding actually works"},"503":{"id":"/docs/stealth#9","page_id":"/docs/stealth","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/stealth#what-this-does-not-hide","content":"What this does not hide"},"504":{"id":"/docs/stealth#10","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth","content":"Root is required for everything else here, so hiding it is a permanent tax. This rig hides the *mechanisms* (su binary, Magisk daemon, Zygisk libs, Frida) rather than trying to make a detector believe the device is unmodified — the attestation layer handles the \"is this a real phone\" question separately."},"505":{"id":"/docs/stealth#11","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#what-is-hidden-and-how","content":"| Mechanism              | Visibility       | Mitigation in this rig                                                 |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `su` binary / `magisk` | filesystem paths | Magisk's own mount/masking; app denylist empty so modules keep working |","table":"table-0"},"506":{"id":"/docs/stealth#12","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#what-is-hidden-and-how","content":"| Mechanism        | Visibility                       | Mitigation in this rig                                    |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Zygisk injection | `/proc/<pid>/maps`, dlopen paths | Zygisk Next `memory-type anonymous` → no file-backed libs |","table":"table-0"},"507":{"id":"/docs/stealth#13","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#what-is-hidden-and-how","content":"| Mechanism     | Visibility              | Mitigation in this rig                          |\n| ------------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| Module mounts | `/proc/<pid>/mountinfo` | only whitelisted apps see them (default policy) |","table":"table-0"},"508":{"id":"/docs/stealth#14","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#what-is-hidden-and-how","content":"| Mechanism | Visibility                                          | Mitigation in this rig                                 |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Frida     | process name, listening port, string `frida-server` | renamed `hluda`, loopback only, no default port on LAN |","table":"table-0"},"509":{"id":"/docs/stealth#15","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#what-is-hidden-and-how","content":"| Mechanism           | Visibility                                 | Mitigation in this rig                |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| Package enumeration | `getPackageInfo` / `queryIntentActivities` | HMA-OSS, scoped per target with `hma` |","table":"table-0"},"510":{"id":"/docs/stealth#16","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#what-is-hidden-and-how","content":"| Mechanism   | Visibility     | Mitigation in this rig                 |\n| ----------- | -------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| Attestation | keystore chain | TrickyStore + keybox (see Attestation) |","table":"table-0"},"511":{"id":"/docs/stealth#17","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#zygisk-next-knobs","content":"`/data/adb/modules/zygisksu/bin/zygiskd` is the control surface:"},"512":{"id":"/docs/stealth#18","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#zygisk-next-knobs","content":"Current config (survives reboot):"},"513":{"id":"/docs/stealth#19","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#the-whitelist-trap","content":"`denylist-policy whitelist` means *only* listed packages get module injection — attractive for stealth, and it **breaks WebView apps**:"},"514":{"id":"/docs/stealth#20","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#the-whitelist-trap","content":"Verified and reverted. Keep `default`, and keep the app you are testing **out** of Magisk's denylist."},"515":{"id":"/docs/stealth#21","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#magisk-denylist-keep-it-empty","content":"If an app is in the denylist, Magisk strips module mounts from it — which is exactly where TrickyStore and PIF need to be. Hiding by denylisting is incompatible with spoofing. Choose one per app."},"516":{"id":"/docs/stealth#22","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#traps","content":"Two-argument form kills `magiskd`; afterwards `magisk -v` says\n`Cannot connect to daemon: Connection refused (os error 111)` and `su` is gone with it. Only a reboot recovers. Always pass a single package argument."},"517":{"id":"/docs/stealth#23","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#traps","content":"There is no stub-repackaging option in Settings and no CLI equivalent. Package-level hiding is HMA-OSS's job; keep that expectation straight when a detector lists installed packages."},"518":{"id":"/docs/stealth#24","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#hma-oss-hiding-packages-from-one-app-at-a-time","content":"HMA-OSS (`hma_oss_zygisk`, manager `org.frknkrc44.hma_oss`) hooks package queries inside a chosen app and filters the answer. It is **scoped per target**: you say \"when *this* app asks, act as if these packages do not exist\"."},"519":{"id":"/docs/stealth#25","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#the-file-that-matters","content":"One JSON document, schema `configVersion: 95`, with a `scope` object keyed by target package. Each entry is an `AppConfig`:"},"520":{"id":"/docs/stealth#26","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#the-file-that-matters","content":"Preset names (they are the module's, not yours): apps = `accessibility_apps, custom_rom, detector_apps, root_apps, shizuku_dhizuku, sus_apps, xposed`; settings = `accessibility, dev_options, input_method`. The five app presets above are what you want against a root-detector: Magisk, KeyAttestation, Frida tooling, other test apps, Xposed-era leftovers."},"521":{"id":"/docs/stealth#27","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#doing-it-from-the-host-not-the-ui","content":"`hma` writes the config in place over `su`, so HMA's `FileObserver(configFile, CLOSE_WRITE or ATTRIB)` picks it up. Logcat then shows `(HMA-Service) Config loaded` (three times per write — `chmod` fires `ATTRIB` as well)."},"522":{"id":"/docs/stealth#28","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#doing-it-from-the-host-not-the-ui","content":"`HMAServiceDataHolder.shouldHideFromUid()` answers from a `uidHideCache` *before* it looks at the config, and only the manager-app pipe clears that cache — the file-reload path does not. Measured: `hma hide` on a live app works immediately (257 → 252 packages, Magisk hidden), `hma unhide` changes the file and nothing else. Reboot to un-hide."},"523":{"id":"/docs/stealth#29","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#doing-it-from-the-host-not-the-ui","content":"If you configure HMA in its UI and press Back, nothing is written — `AppSettingsV2Fragment` persists in `onPause`. Press HOME (or leave the app) to commit. This is why hand-editing `config.json` with `hma` is the less surprising path."},"524":{"id":"/docs/stealth#30","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#doing-it-from-the-host-not-the-ui","content":"The `FileObserver` is constructed at boot even when the file is missing. If HMA has never written a config on this boot, your first `hma hide` needs one reboot before it has any effect. Check with `hma show` — if it is empty and you just created a scope, reboot, then re-apply."},"525":{"id":"/docs/stealth#31","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#verifying-hiding-actually-works","content":"**Measure with an app that declares `QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES`.** Without it, Android 11+ package-visibility filtering makes every app look clean:"},"526":{"id":"/docs/stealth#32","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#verifying-hiding-actually-works","content":"Use `apks/ApplistDetector.V2.4.apk` (`icu.nullptr.applistdetector`, Dr-TSNG) as the detector:"},"527":{"id":"/docs/stealth#33","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#verifying-hiding-actually-works","content":"Measured on this rig, detector scoped, before vs after reboot:"},"528":{"id":"/docs/stealth#34","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#verifying-hiding-actually-works","content":"| state              | installed count | `com.topjohnwu.magisk` |\n| ------------------ | --------------- | ---------------------- |\n| baseline, no scope | 256             | visible                |","table":"table-1"},"529":{"id":"/docs/stealth#35","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#verifying-hiding-actually-works","content":"| state           | installed count | `com.topjohnwu.magisk` |\n| --------------- | --------------- | ---------------------- |\n| scoped + reboot | 252             | hidden                 |","table":"table-1"},"530":{"id":"/docs/stealth#36","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#verifying-hiding-actually-works","content":"| state                     | installed count | `com.topjohnwu.magisk`             |\n| ------------------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| live-added scope (Chrome) | 257 → 252       | visible → hidden, no reboot needed |","table":"table-1"},"531":{"id":"/docs/stealth#37","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#verifying-hiding-actually-works","content":"HMA never hides a target app from itself, so the detector still lists `icu.nullptr.applistdetector` — that is correct behaviour, not a leak."},"532":{"id":"/docs/stealth#38","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#verifying-hiding-actually-works","content":"Hiding does not disturb spoofing: after HMA was enabled, KeyAttestation still reported the keybox chain (`CN=Droid CA2, O=Google LLC`) and `Bootloader is locked`."},"533":{"id":"/docs/stealth#39","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#verifying-hiding-actually-works","content":"The 10-mount difference is the honest answer to \"is injection scoped\": non-target apps see zero module mounts."},"534":{"id":"/docs/stealth#40","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#what-this-does-not-hide","content":"**Emulator fingerprints** (`ro.kernel.qemu`, `goldfish` hardware, sensor set). Apps that check them are dealt with by `intercept`'s root/emulator detection bypass, not by this layer."},"535":{"id":"/docs/stealth#41","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#what-this-does-not-hide","content":"**A keybox that is revoked** — that is server-side truth, see Attestation."},"536":{"id":"/docs/stealth#42","page_id":"/docs/stealth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/stealth#what-this-does-not-hide","content":"**Your traffic** — it leaves from the host's IP through mitmproxy."},"537":{"id":"/docs/tooling","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"page","content":"Command reference","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Tools"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling"},"538":{"id":"/docs/tooling#0","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#health--control","content":"Health & control"},"539":{"id":"/docs/tooling#1","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#pentestctl","content":"`pentestctl`"},"540":{"id":"/docs/tooling#2","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#nettap","content":"`nettap`"},"541":{"id":"/docs/tooling#3","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#snap","content":"`snap`"},"542":{"id":"/docs/tooling#4","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#frida","content":"Frida"},"543":{"id":"/docs/tooling#5","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#fspawn-pkg-profile-frida-args","content":"`fspawn <pkg> [profile] [frida args…]`"},"544":{"id":"/docs/tooling#6","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#fdp-pkg-port","content":"`fdp [pkg] [port]`"},"545":{"id":"/docs/tooling#7","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#cdp-urleval-jswatch-secs","content":"`cdp url|eval \"<js>\"|watch [secs]`"},"546":{"id":"/docs/tooling#8","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#session","content":"`session`"},"547":{"id":"/docs/tooling#9","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#medusa-export","content":"`medusa-export`"},"548":{"id":"/docs/tooling#10","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#traffic","content":"Traffic"},"549":{"id":"/docs/tooling#11","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#replay","content":"`replay`"},"550":{"id":"/docs/tooling#12","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#recon","content":"`recon`"},"551":{"id":"/docs/tooling#13","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#entry","content":"`entry`"},"552":{"id":"/docs/tooling#14","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#pull-data","content":"`pull-data`"},"553":{"id":"/docs/tooling#15","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#attestation-integrity-and-hiding","content":"Attestation, integrity and hiding"},"554":{"id":"/docs/tooling#16","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#setup-keyboxsh--keybox-refresh","content":"`setup-keybox.sh` / `keybox-refresh`"},"555":{"id":"/docs/tooling#17","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#hma","content":"`hma`"},"556":{"id":"/docs/tooling#18","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#integrity","content":"`integrity`"},"557":{"id":"/docs/tooling#19","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#device-helpers","content":"Device helpers"},"558":{"id":"/docs/tooling#20","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#asu","content":"`asu`"},"559":{"id":"/docs/tooling#21","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#uitap","content":"`uitap`"},"560":{"id":"/docs/tooling#22","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#apktool","content":"`apktool`"},"561":{"id":"/docs/tooling#23","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#docs","content":"`docs`"},"562":{"id":"/docs/tooling#24","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#host-environment","content":"Host environment"},"563":{"id":"/docs/tooling#25","page_id":"/docs/tooling","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/tooling#cheat-sheet","content":"Cheat sheet"},"564":{"id":"/docs/tooling#26","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling","content":"Everything is in `~/mobsec/bin` (already on `PATH`). All commands assume the emulator is running."},"565":{"id":"/docs/tooling#27","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#pentestctl","content":"Sections and what they read:"},"566":{"id":"/docs/tooling#28","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#pentestctl","content":"| Section | Source of truth     |\n| ------- | ------------------- |\n| device  | `adb shell getprop` |","table":"table-0"},"567":{"id":"/docs/tooling#29","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#pentestctl","content":"| Section | Source of truth               |\n| ------- | ----------------------------- |\n| root    | `su -c id`, `su -c magisk -v` |","table":"table-0"},"568":{"id":"/docs/tooling#30","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#pentestctl","content":"| Section | Source of truth  |\n| ------- | ---------------- |\n| zygisk  | `zygiskd status` |","table":"table-0"},"569":{"id":"/docs/tooling#31","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#pentestctl","content":"| Section     | Source of truth                                                 |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| attestation | `/data/adb/tricky_store/{keybox.xml,target.txt}` + `kbcheck.py` |","table":"table-0"},"570":{"id":"/docs/tooling#32","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#pentestctl","content":"| Section | Source of truth             |\n| ------- | --------------------------- |\n| frida   | `/data/adb/fsrv/ctl status` |","table":"table-0"},"571":{"id":"/docs/tooling#33","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#pentestctl","content":"| Section      | Source of truth                                                                                     |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| interception | `/tmp/mitm.pid`, `adb reverse --list`, `settings get global http_proxy`, flow count, cert-fixer log |","table":"table-0"},"572":{"id":"/docs/tooling#34","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#nettap","content":"Env: `ADDON` (dump.py), `FLOWDIR`, `INTEREST`, `PORT`. `nettap on` refuses to start if the addon or `mitmdump` is missing instead of dying silently."},"573":{"id":"/docs/tooling#35","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#fspawn-pkg-profile-frida-args","content":"Profiles: `trace` (default), `web`, `attest`, `spy`, `intercept`, `full`, `raw`. See Frida."},"574":{"id":"/docs/tooling#36","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#fdp-pkg-port","content":"Finds `webview_devtools_remote_<pid>` in `/proc/net/unix` (auto-detects the foreground app when `pkg` is omitted), forwards `:9222`, prints the target list."},"575":{"id":"/docs/tooling#37","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#cdp-urleval-jswatch-secs","content":"Minimal CDP client (python3 + `websockets`). `eval` awaits promises; `watch` streams console/network events."},"576":{"id":"/docs/tooling#38","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#session","content":"Merges `document.cookie`, `localStorage`, `sessionStorage` from the WebView with the newest flow's cookie header (httpOnly cookies are invisible to JS). `TARGET=target session` restricts the page match."},"577":{"id":"/docs/tooling#39","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#replay","content":"Defaults to exactly what the app sent (same headers, cookie, body). `-x` sends through mitmproxy (captured as evidence). `--save` writes the response body."},"578":{"id":"/docs/tooling#40","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#recon","content":"Writes `~/.mobsec/recon/<pkg>-<ts>/report.md` + `raw/`. See Static recon."},"579":{"id":"/docs/tooling#41","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#entry","content":"Turns the manifest into copy-paste attack commands — one `adb shell am start|broadcast|content` line per exported component and deep link."},"580":{"id":"/docs/tooling#42","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#entry","content":"The sheet lists exported activities/services/receivers with their required permissions, content providers (including `exported=false` + `grantUriPermissions=true`), every `scheme://host` deep link, and `pm get-app-links` state."},"581":{"id":"/docs/tooling#43","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#pull-data","content":"The honest replacement for `adb backup` (blocked on API 31+): root-tars the app's private dir, pulls it, and summarises."},"582":{"id":"/docs/tooling#44","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#pull-data","content":"Reports the biggest files, every SQLite database with tables/row counts, `shared_prefs` and JSON lines that look like secrets, and pulls `/sdcard/Android/data/<pkg>` too. Writes `summary.txt` next to the extracted tree."},"583":{"id":"/docs/tooling#45","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#setup-keyboxsh--keybox-refresh","content":"`keybox-refresh` refreshes automatically only when the leaf is close to expiry or revoked, validates candidates with `kbcheck.py --strict`, and backs up the old keybox. It is wired to a systemd user timer. See Attestation."},"584":{"id":"/docs/tooling#46","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#hma","content":"Root-hiding scope editor for HMA-OSS (writes `config.json` over `su`, reloads live)."},"585":{"id":"/docs/tooling#47","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#hma","content":"Un-hiding needs a reboot (uid cache); a `config.json` created *after* boot needs one reboot before it is watched. See Root hiding."},"586":{"id":"/docs/tooling#48","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#integrity","content":"Play Integrity verdict from SPIC, scraped out of logcat."},"587":{"id":"/docs/tooling#49","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#integrity","content":"Expect `UNEVALUATED` on this AVD — it is Google declining to grade an emulator with no account, not a rig failure. See Play Integrity."},"588":{"id":"/docs/tooling#50","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#asu","content":"Runs a root shell snippet without the `adb shell su -c \"…\"` quoting nightmare:"},"589":{"id":"/docs/tooling#51","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#uitap","content":"Text-driven UI automation (`uiautomator dump` under the hood) — survives layout changes that break fixed coordinates:"},"590":{"id":"/docs/tooling#52","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#apktool","content":"Wrapper around the pinned `apktool_3.0.3.jar` (`apktool d app.apk -o out`)."},"591":{"id":"/docs/tooling#53","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#docs","content":"The documentation site you are reading, served locally."},"592":{"id":"/docs/tooling#54","page_id":"/docs/tooling","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/tooling#docs","content":"For permanent LAN sharing there is a user unit, `mobsec-docs.service`\n(`systemctl --user enable --now mobsec-docs`), and `sudo ufw allow 8000/tcp` once — `ufw`'s default\ninbound policy is `DROP`, so a bound port is not a reachable port."},"593":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting"},"594":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#0","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-five-minute-triage","content":"The five-minute triage"},"595":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#1","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"Symptom → cause"},"596":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#2","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#trap-list-all-hit-for-real-here","content":"Trap list (all hit for real here)"},"597":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#3","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#1-adb-reverse-does-not-survive-a-reboot","content":"1. `adb reverse` does not survive a reboot"},"598":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#4","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#2-frida---devnull-exits-instantly","content":"2. `frida … < /dev/null` exits instantly"},"599":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#5","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#3-pkill--f-kills-your-own-shell","content":"3. `pkill -f` kills your own shell"},"600":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#6","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#4-magisk---denylist-rm-pkg-process-segfaults-magiskd","content":"4. `magisk --denylist rm <pkg> <process>` segfaults magiskd"},"601":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#7","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#5-whitelist-denylist-policy-breaks-webview-renderers","content":"5. Whitelist denylist policy breaks WebView renderers"},"602":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#8","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#6-adb-shell-su--c--mangles-quotes-and-loops","content":"6. `adb shell su -c '…'` mangles quotes and loops"},"603":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#9","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#7-dont-grep-dataadbmoduleszygisksu-recursively","content":"7. Don't grep `/data/adb/modules/zygisksu/` recursively"},"604":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#10","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#8-mitmproxy-does-not-hot-reload-addons","content":"8. mitmproxy does not hot-reload addons"},"605":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#11","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#9-playintegrityfork-v19-is-arm-only","content":"9. PlayIntegrityFork v19 is arm-only"},"606":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#12","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#10-medusas-shared_preferences-module-kills-webview-apps","content":"10. Medusa's `shared_preferences` module kills WebView apps"},"607":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#13","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#recovery-runbook","content":"Recovery runbook"},"608":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#14","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#logs-worth-knowing","content":"Logs worth knowing"},"609":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#15","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#when-nothing-makes-sense","content":"When nothing makes sense"},"610":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#16","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Ordered by how often each one actually happens."},"611":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#17","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-five-minute-triage","content":"If `pentestctl status` is green but the app is silent, the problem is almost always **inside the app** (dead proxy in a cached connection, app not restarted, wrong package)."},"612":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#18","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                       | Most likely cause            | Fix         |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ----------- |\n| App spins forever, zero flows | `adb reverse` died on reboot | `nettap on` |","table":"table-0"},"613":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#19","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                                | Most likely cause            | Fix                                         |\n| -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| Zero flows but `nettap status` says up | app cached a dead connection | force-stop + relaunch; `fspawn … intercept` |","table":"table-0"},"614":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#20","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                                      | Most likely cause               | Fix                                                 |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| GMS/Play Store TLS errors in `/tmp/mitm.log` | Cert-Fixer didn't run this boot | reboot, then `pentestctl status \\| grep Cert-Fixer` |","table":"table-0"},"615":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#21","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                                 | Most likely cause | Fix                                          |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `frida-ps` hangs or \"unable to connect\" | frida-server died | `adb shell su -c '/data/adb/fsrv/ctl start'` |","table":"table-0"},"616":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#22","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                                 | Most likely cause                 | Fix                                          |\n| --------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `Failed to spawn` but package installed | wrong package name / user profile | `adb shell pm list packages \\| grep -i name` |","table":"table-0"},"617":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#23","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                            | Most likely cause | Fix                                           |\n| ---------------------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| App crashes at startup under Frida | a script broke it | `fspawn <pkg> raw`, add scripts one at a time |","table":"table-0"},"618":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#24","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                                | Most likely cause         | Fix                                           |\n| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `net_error -202` on every WebView page | whitelist denylist policy | `zygiskd denylist-policy default` (see below) |","table":"table-0"},"619":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#25","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                                             | Most likely cause                                           | Fix                                                             |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Attestation rejected (`4202`) after a keybox change | `target.txt` missing the package, or keybox revoked/expired | `pentestctl status \\| grep keybox`, add package, force-stop app |","table":"table-0"},"620":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#26","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                                  | Most likely cause                              | Fix    |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `magisk -v` → `Cannot connect to daemon` | daemon segfaulted by a two-arg `--denylist rm` | reboot |","table":"table-0"},"621":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#27","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                                  | Most likely cause                | Fix                                               |\n| ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| Emulator won't boot after a bad snapshot | snapshot captured a broken mount | `snap boot` (cold), verify, `snap save <newname>` |","table":"table-0"},"622":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#28","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#symptom--cause","content":"| Symptom                                            | Most likely cause                               | Fix                                                      |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A command you rely on suddenly behaves differently | a `~/mobsec/bin` helper shadows it (PATH order) | `pentestctl status` → *host commands*; rename the helper |","table":"table-0"},"623":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#29","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#1-adb-reverse-does-not-survive-a-reboot","content":"`settings put global http_proxy` **does**. Result: the app points at `127.0.0.1:18080` where nothing listens, and every request hangs with no error. `pentestctl fix` handles it."},"624":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#30","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#2-frida---devnull-exits-instantly","content":"No tty → REPL dies. Use a fifo:"},"625":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#31","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#3-pkill--f-kills-your-own-shell","content":"`pkill -f qemu-system` or `pkill -f 'frida -U -f pkg'` matches the `bash -c \"<that command>\"` wrapper and kills the invoking shell (exit 143). Record the PID and `kill <pid>`."},"626":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#32","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#4-magisk---denylist-rm-pkg-process-segfaults-magiskd","content":"Always one argument: `magisk --denylist rm <pkg>`. Recovery from the crash requires a reboot."},"627":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#33","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#5-whitelist-denylist-policy-breaks-webview-renderers","content":"`zygiskd denylist-policy whitelist` avoids injecting into non-listed apps, but renderer sandbox processes (`…:sandboxed_process0`, isolated uid) never match the package, so the CA and unpinning hooks are missing inside WebView → `SSL handshake failed; net_error -202`. Keep `default`."},"628":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#34","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#6-adb-shell-su--c--mangles-quotes-and-loops","content":"Multi-line snippets with `for`/`while` fail with `syntax error: unexpected 'do'`. Use `asu '…'`, which writes a script and runs it."},"629":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#35","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#7-dont-grep-dataadbmoduleszygisksu-recursively","content":"Its webroot has megabytes of i18n JSON and floods your terminal (and your context). Read specific files."},"630":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#36","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#8-mitmproxy-does-not-hot-reload-addons","content":"Edited `mitm/dump.py`? `nettap off && nettap on`, otherwise you keep the old behaviour (this is how a \"fixed\" filename bug appears unfixed)."},"631":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#37","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#9-playintegrityfork-v19-is-arm-only","content":"On x86_64 it silently never loads (`zygiskd status` stops listing `playintegrityfix`). Use the 4.9 x86_64 build."},"632":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#38","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#10-medusas-shared_preferences-module-kills-webview-apps","content":"`java.lang.NullPointerException … SharedPreferences$Editor.apply() on a null object reference` inside `WebViewChromiumFactoryProvider`. Not in any default profile."},"633":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#39","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#recovery-runbook","content":"If step 5 is stale, reboot once — Cert-Fixer only mounts at `post-fs-data`."},"634":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#40","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#logs-worth-knowing","content":"| Log             | What                                                   |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `/tmp/mitm.log` | mitmdump stdout (`-v`), TLS failures, addon exceptions |","table":"table-1"},"635":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#41","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#logs-worth-knowing","content":"| Log                     | What                 |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------- |\n| `/tmp/mtflows/_err.log` | addon write failures |","table":"table-1"},"636":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#42","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#logs-worth-knowing","content":"| Log              | What                                        |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `/tmp/frida.log` | your `fspawn` output when run in background |","table":"table-1"},"637":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#43","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#logs-worth-knowing","content":"| Log                              | What                     |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `/data/local/tmp/cert-fixer.log` | CA mount result per boot |","table":"table-1"},"638":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#44","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#logs-worth-knowing","content":"| Log          | What                                                                  |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `adb logcat` | app crashes: `adb logcat -v time \\| grep -iE 'AndroidRuntime\\|FATAL'` |","table":"table-1"},"639":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#45","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#when-nothing-makes-sense","content":"Compare against a state you know worked:"},"640":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting#46","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#when-nothing-makes-sense","content":"If the demo app also fails, the rig is broken. If only your target fails, the target has an additional defence — collect `fspawn … trace` output and read the `rootcheck`/`tls` lines before guessing."},"641":{"id":"/docs/workflow","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"page","content":"Daily workflow","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow"},"642":{"id":"/docs/workflow#0","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#1-restore-a-known-good-state","content":"1. Restore a known-good state"},"643":{"id":"/docs/workflow#1","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#2-start-the-capture","content":"2. Start the capture"},"644":{"id":"/docs/workflow#2","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#3-instrument-dont-guess","content":"3. Instrument, don't guess"},"645":{"id":"/docs/workflow#3","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#4-capture-what-the-app-sends","content":"4. Capture what the app sends"},"646":{"id":"/docs/workflow#4","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#5-replay-with-intent","content":"5. Replay with intent"},"647":{"id":"/docs/workflow#5","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#6-document-as-you-go","content":"6. Document as you go"},"648":{"id":"/docs/workflow#6","page_id":"/docs/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workflow#session-hygiene","content":"Session hygiene"},"649":{"id":"/docs/workflow#7","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow","content":"The loop that matters: **restore → verify → instrument → capture → replay → document.**"},"650":{"id":"/docs/workflow#8","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#1-restore-a-known-good-state","content":"If you changed anything device-wide (new module, new CA, new keybox), `snap save` a **new** snapshot name instead of overwriting `logged-in` — snapshots carry the mount state, and a stale snapshot can bring back a broken CA mount."},"651":{"id":"/docs/workflow#9","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#2-start-the-capture","content":"`nettap on` is idempotent. For pinned apps you can even drop the global proxy afterwards (`adb shell settings put global http_proxy :0`) — `fspawn … intercept` redirects connections in-process, so capture continues."},"652":{"id":"/docs/workflow#10","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#3-instrument-dont-guess","content":"Rules of thumb:"},"653":{"id":"/docs/workflow#11","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#3-instrument-dont-guess","content":"**WebView/Tauri/Cordova app?** You get 80% of the answer from `fdp` + `cdp eval` — DOM, storage, fetch wrappers, console. Do that before native hooking."},"654":{"id":"/docs/workflow#12","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#3-instrument-dont-guess","content":"**Native pinning / keystore work?** `intercept` first, then `trace`, then `full`."},"655":{"id":"/docs/workflow#13","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#3-instrument-dont-guess","content":"**Frida REPL needs a tty.** Backgrounded `frida` dies instantly if stdin is `/dev/null`; use a fifo (see Frida)."},"656":{"id":"/docs/workflow#14","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#4-capture-what-the-app-sends","content":"Flows are `<HHMMSS>_<host>_<path>.txt` with request headers/body and response headers/body, plus a machine-readable `_index.jsonl`. Full format: Flows."},"657":{"id":"/docs/workflow#15","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#5-replay-with-intent","content":"`--dry` prints the exact request without sending — use it every time before a `--patch`. `-x` sends through mitmproxy so the attempt is captured as evidence."},"658":{"id":"/docs/workflow#16","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#6-document-as-you-go","content":"Then write findings with the evidence pointer (`flow file`, `timestamp`, `endpoint`, `repro command`). A finding without a repro command is a rumour."},"659":{"id":"/docs/workflow#17","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflow#session-hygiene","content":"**One app at a time** on the emulator: `fdp` binds `:9222` and `fspawn` force-stops the package."},"660":{"id":"/docs/workflow#18","page_id":"/docs/workflow","tags":[],"type":"tex