oid-proxy-override.js`** — rewrites `System.getProperty(\"http.proxyHost\")`, `ConnectivityManager.getDefaultProxy()` and OkHttp's proxy selector."],[372,"**`bootstrap.sh` / `fetch-deps.sh` / `install-device.sh` / `setup-keybox.sh` / `setup-net.sh`** — the automated path, in that order."],[371,"**`GUIDE-from-scratch.md`** — the narrative walkthrough (12 sections, beginner-friendly, includes the interactive Magisk UI steps and every download URL)."],[325,"**`native-connect-hook.js` / `native-tls-hook.js`** — LD_PRELOAD-style hooks (`connect`, `getaddrinfo`, `SSL_*`) so native code (Rust/Flutter/Go) also goes through the proxy and trusts our CA."],[249,"**`Zygisk-Assistant`** — popular root-hiding module. Not used: it requires targets in Magisk's denylist, which strips our spoofing modules from those same apps."],[535,"**A keybox that is revoked** — that is server-side truth, see Attestation."],[451,"**A snapshot is only as logged-in as the moment you saved it.** After `keybox-refresh` rotates the\nkeybox, the device presents a new attestation identity on the next launch and the backend drops the\nsession — a snapshot saved before the rotation restores a logged-out app. Re-login (you need the\nTOTP), then `snap save logged-in` again."],[222,"**adb reverse** — forwards a port on the *device* to the host. Used so the app can reach mitmproxy on `127.0.0.1:18080` without a LAN proxy. Dies on every reboot."],[223,"**Attestation chain** — certificate chain returned by the Android keystore for a generated key: leaf (app key) → TEE intermediate → Droid CA → Google root. Encodes device identity, lock state and verified-boot status."],[176,"**Attestation-friendly**: capture the login once, replay everything else; you never need a fresh keystore challenge for non-login endpoints."],[224,"**AVD** — Android Virtual Device. Here: `pentest16`, pixel_7 profile, API 36 Play Store image."],[225,"**Bootloader locked / verified boot** — properties the server can read from the attestation extension. TrickyStore's keybox decides what the server sees."],[315,"**CA trust** — the mitmproxy CA is installed as a *user* CA (`/data/misc/user/0/cacerts-added/<hash>.0`) and then mounted into the system trust store by **Cert-Fixer** at boot."],[316,"**Capture** — `mitm/dump.py` writes one file per interesting flow."],[226,"**CDP** — Chrome DevTools Protocol. Over `adb forward :9222` it gives DOM, console, storage and network for any debuggable WebView."],[227,"**Cert-Fixer** — Magisk module that bind-mounts user CAs into `/apex/com.android.conscrypt/cacerts` at `post-fs-data`, so system apps (GMS, Play Store) trust mitmproxy."],[29,"**Cert-Fixer** mounts the CA at boot for the *whole system*, which is why Play Store and GMS traffic decrypts instead of failing with `does not trust the proxy's certificate`."],[298,"**Check it is really PI.** If the app also sends a key-attestation chain (Tauri/Rust/native apps often do), the keybox path already covers you — Target is exactly this case."],[228,"**conscrypt** — Android's TLS provider and the place the system trust store lives since Android 14 (moved out of `/system/etc/security/cacerts`)."],[229,"**denylist (Magisk)** — packages that get *no* module injection. Empty in this rig on purpose: TrickyStore/PIF must reach the target app."],[230,"**denylist policy (Zygisk Next)** — `default` (inject everywhere except denylisted) or `whitelist` (inject only listed). Whitelist breaks WebView renderer sandboxes."],[38,"**Denylist policy `default`, not `whitelist`** — whitelist mode injects only for listed packages, but WebView renderer sandbox processes (`…:sandboxed_process0`, isolated uid) never match the package name, so every page load failed with `net_error -202`. Tried it, reverted it; see Root hiding."],[534,"**Emulator fingerprints** (`ro.kernel.qemu`, `goldfish` hardware, sensor set). Apps that check them are dealt with by `intercept`'s root/emulator detection bypass, not by this layer."],[177,"**Evidence-friendly**: `-x` re-sends through mitmproxy, so the attempt lands in the same flow corpus with a timestamp."],[655,"**Frida REPL needs a tty.** Backgrounded `frida` dies instantly if stdin is `/dev/null`; use a fifo (see Frida)."],[299,"**Frida-hook the client side.** `IntegrityManager.requestIntegrityToken` / the verdict parser in the app: hook the callback and hand back a verdict the app likes. Works only when the backend trusts the *client* to inspect the verdict, which is a bug worth reporting in itself."],[39,"**frida-server, not gadget** — gadget needs per-APK patching and re-signing, which changes the APK signature (and some servers check it). Server-side injection leaves the APK untouched."],[231,"**frida-server** — the on-device agent. Here renamed `hluda`, autostarted by the `fsrv` Magisk module, listening on loopback only."],[232,"**gadget** — Frida's injectable library for non-rooted devices; requires patching and re-signing the APK, which changes its signature. Not used here."],[314,"**Global proxy** `127.0.0.1:18080` (optional once `fspawn intercept` is in play)."],[233,"**HMA-OSS** — \"Hide My Applist\" fork: hides installed packages from a target app's enumeration. Installed, hide list empty."],[356,"**It is bound to `0.0.0.0`**, not `127.0.0.1` (`docs serve --lan` does that; `docs status` shows the bind)."],[235,"**keybox revocation list** — Google's published serial blacklist at `android.googleapis.com/attestation/status`. Server-side check; cannot be spoofed locally."],[234,"**keybox.xml** — TrickyStore's replacement cert+key material: EC and/or RSA chains plus private keys. Must be hardware (RKP), unexpired and unrevoked."],[236,"**KVM** — kernel virtual machine; `/dev/kvm` + `kvm` group membership makes the emulator usable."],[40,"**Loopback-only frida** — `LISTEN=127.0.0.1:27042` + `adb` forwarding. Nothing on the LAN can reach the agent, and no `frida-server` string appears in a listening-socket scan."],[237,"**Magisk** — systemless root. Version 31.1 here, applied to the system image's ramdisk via rootAVD."],[525,"**Measure with an app that declares `QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES`.** Without it, Android 11+ package-visibility filtering makes every app look clean:"],[238,"**mitmproxy / mitmdump** — the intercepting proxy. `mitm/dump.py` addon writes one file per flow."],[654,"**Native pinning / keystore work?** `intercept` first, then `trace`, then `full`."],[659,"**One app at a time** on the emulator: `fdp` binds `:9222` and `fspawn` force-stops the package."],[240,"**PIF (PlayIntegrityFix)** — module that tries to satisfy PI by spoofing props; on an emulator it still fails."],[239,"**Play Integrity (PI)** — Google's app-level integrity API (device/app/account verdicts). Emulator → `NO_INTEGRITY`; not solvable here."],[37,"**Play Store image over AOSP** — closer to a real device for attestation checks; the cost is a heavier boot and GMS noise in every capture (filtered by `IGNORE` in `dump.py`)."],[293,"**PlayIntegrityFix 4.9** (`playintegrityfix`) patches device props in GMS's process so DroidGuard is less likely to notice the emulator. It is installed and loading (`zygiskd status` lists it) — it just cannot manufacture a device verdict that Google refuses to issue."],[294,"**PlayIntegrityFork v19** is parked in `modules/archive/`: it ships **only** `arm64-v8a` and `armeabi-v7a` Zygisk libs, so on this x86_64 image it silently never loads. Watch for that class of bug with `zygiskd status` after every module change — the module staying absent from `modules64:` is the tell."],[241,"**post-fs-data** — earliest Magisk boot stage; where Cert-Fixer mounts CAs."],[300,"**Replay with a good token.** `session` + `replay` let you re-issue the request with a token minted on a clean device — that is the same thing a real attacker does, and it demonstrates the missing server-side binding."],[242,"**RKP** — Remote Key Provisioning. Modern hardware attestation where keys/certs are provisioned by Google per device."],[243,"**rootAVD** — script that patches an AVD's `ramdisk.img` with Magisk; modifies the system image, not the AVD config."],[175,"**Same headers** as the app, including device-specific ones and the cookie jar state at capture time."],[244,"**snapshot (AVD)** — full VM state save/restore (`adb emu avd snapshot save`). ~5 GB, ~25 s restore."],[246,"**TEE** — Trusted Execution Environment; hardware side that produces attestation. Emulators fake it (`teeBroken=true`)."],[296,"**TEESimulator** (JingMatrix, GPL-3.0) is the current community answer: a software KeyMint that needs a keybox, designed for exactly this \"make a non-device look like a device\" problem. It is a candidate upgrade for this rig; it is not installed, and it would still be fighting Play's verdict rather than key attestation."],[357,"**The host firewall lets the port in.** On a box with `ufw` enabled the default inbound policy is\n`DROP`, so once:"],[245,"**TrickyStore** — Zygisk module that substitutes keystore attestation chains for packages in `target.txt` using `keybox.xml`."],[295,"**TrickyStore** fakes the keystore chain. Play Integrity's `STRONG_INTEGRITY` needs a hardware-backed signature over the *app signing key* by a Google-trusted root — key attestation spoofing gets you partway, then Google's own evaluation of the resulting record is the wall."],[301,"**Use a physical device.** No emulator configuration passes `MEETS_DEVICE_INTEGRITY`; that is the point of the product."],[653,"**WebView/Tauri/Cordova app?** You get 80% of the answer from `fdp` + `cdp eval` — DOM, storage, fetch wrappers, console. Do that before native hooking."],[536,"**Your traffic** — it leaves from the host's IP through mitmproxy."],[247,"**Zygisk** — Magisk's code-injection mechanism into zygote-spawned apps. Disabled in Magisk itself here; **Zygisk Next** provides it."],[248,"**zygiskd** — Zygisk Next's control CLI (`status`, `enforce-denylist`, `denylist-policy`, `memory-type`)."],[425,"`--deep` decompiles with jadx (1.5.7) and greps string literals for URLs, then writes `endpoints.txt`. Use it to build the API list before you even launch the app; combine with the captured flows later."],[657,"`--dry` prints the exact request without sending — use it every time before a `--patch`. `-x` sends through mitmproxy so the attempt is captured as evidence."],[440,"`-no-snapshot-save` is deliberate: when the emulator exits it would otherwise overwrite the snapshot with whatever half-broken state you were in."],[511,"`/data/adb/modules/zygisksu/bin/zygiskd` is the control surface:"],[560,"`apktool`"],[558,"`asu`"],[545,"`cdp url|eval \"<js>\"|watch [secs]`"],[513,"`denylist-policy whitelist` means *only* listed packages get module injection — attractive for stealth, and it **breaks WebView apps**:"],[561,"`docs`"],[551,"`entry`"],[544,"`fdp [pkg] [port]`"],[333,"`FLOWDIR` (default `/tmp/mtflows`), `INTEREST` (only matching URLs), `IGNORE` (default drops googleapis/gstatic/ggbn/firebase/app-measurement/crashlytics noise), `MAXBODY` (20000 bytes per body)."],[197,"`frida` + `frida-tools` 17.27.5 (pipx), `objection` available for quick jobs, and these wrappers:"],[543,"`fspawn <pkg> [profile] [frida args…]`"],[420,"`Google_API_Key` / `Firebase` keys are **usually not secrets** — they are restricted by package name + SHA-1. Report only if a restriction test shows otherwise."],[555,"`hma`"],[521,"`hma` writes the config in place over `su`, so HMA's `FileObserver(configFile, CLOSE_WRITE or ATTRIB)` picks it up. Logcat then shows `(HMA-Service) Config loaded` (three times per write — `chmod` fires `ATTRIB` as well)."],[522,"`HMAServiceDataHolder.shouldHideFromUid()` answers from a `uidHideCache` *before* it looks at the config, and only the manager-app pipe clears that cache — the file-reload path does not. Measured: `hma hide` on a live app works immediately (257 → 252 packages, Magisk hidden), `hma unhide` changes the file and nothing else. Reboot to un-hide."],[379,"`install-device.sh` finishes with a reboot; wait for `adb wait-for-device` before continuing."],[556,"`integrity`"],[288,"`integrity` drives **SPIC** (`com.henrikherzig.playintegritychecker`, in `apks/`): force-stops it, launches it, finds the \"Make Play Integrity Request\" button via `uiautomator dump`, taps it, and parses the JSON block SPIC prints to `I/System.out` (that is where the library dumps the token payload)."],[632,"`java.lang.NullPointerException … SharedPreferences$Editor.apply() on a null object reference` inside `WebViewChromiumFactoryProvider`. Not in any default profile."],[583,"`keybox-refresh` refreshes automatically only when the leaf is close to expiry or revoked, validates candidates with `kbcheck.py --strict`, and backs up the old keybox. It is wired to a systemd user timer. See Attestation."],[55,"`keybox.xml` — the replacement chain material (EC and/or RSA), plus the private keys that let the keystore actually sign with it."],[452,"`load`/`boot` start the emulator with `-no-snapshot-save` so a broken session cannot overwrite a\ngood snapshot. The emulator reports the refusal as `UNSUPPORTED_VK_APP`, which looks like a GPU\nproblem and is not. `snap save <name> --reopen` cold-boots keeping `/data`, then saves."],[18,"`magisk --denylist rm <pkg> <process>` (two args) **segfaults the daemon**. Use one argument."],[547,"`medusa-export`"],[651,"`nettap on` is idempotent. For pinned apps you can even drop the global proxy afterwards (`adb shell settings put global http_proxy :0`) — `fspawn … intercept` redirects connections in-process, so capture continues."],[540,"`nettap`"],[415,"`p003a2/v.java` → Material `MaterialAutoCompleteTextView` (a Meizu hint workaround)"],[417,"`p019g/A.java` → `!\"robolectric\".equals(Build.FINGERPRINT)`"],[416,"`p045n1/k.java` → GMS `DialogRedirect` logging"],[12,"`pentest16` is a **Play Store** (`google_apis_playstore`) system image for API 36, x86_64, pixel_7 profile, 6 GB RAM, 16 GB data partition. Play Store matters: several attestation-ish code paths check for GMS presence and behave differently without it."],[539,"`pentestctl`"],[30,"`pentestctl` (health), `nettap` (proxy+tunnel+addon), `fspawn` (spawn under Frida with a profile), `fdp`/`cdp` (WebView DevTools), `session` (harvest cookies+storage), `replay` (re-issue requests), `recon` (static APK), `snap` (AVD snapshots), `uitap` (UI automation), `asu` (run root snippets)."],[625,"`pkill -f qemu-system` or `pkill -f 'frida -U -f pkg'` matches the `bash -c \"<that command>\"` wrapper and kills the invoking shell (exit 143). Record the PID and `kill <pid>`."],[89,"`PlayIntegrityFork` v19 ships only arm64/armv7 `zygisk` libs, so on this x86_64 image it silently never loads (`zygiskd status` stops listing `playintegrityfix`). The installed module is `PlayIntegrityFix_v4.9-inject-s.zip`, which does ship x86_64. v19 is parked in `modules/archive/`."],[552,"`pull-data`"],[426,"`recon com.example.app --deep` — components, permissions, endpoints, secrets."],[550,"`recon`"],[431,"`recon` is a shell script; every step is independent (`aapt2`, `apkanalyzer`, `apkid`, `apkleaks`, `mobsfscan`, `jadx`). Add steps by copying the pattern in `~/mobsec/bin/recon` — each writes into `raw/` and appends a section to `report.md`."],[549,"`replay`"],[172,"`replay` re-issues a captured request from the host, defaulting to *exactly* what the app sent, with explicit overrides:"],[65,"`root=None` is normal: the bundled root bundle (`tools/keybox-res/`) predates the RKP root (`CN=Key Attestation CA1`), so the root *pin* cannot be matched — signatures and revocation still validate, and the server is the real judge."],[14,"`rootAVD` patches `ramdisk.img` of the **system image** (not the AVD) with Magisk, then the Magisk app does a second \"additional setup\" pass on first boot. Result: `su` works, `context=u:r:magisk:s0`."],[546,"`session`"],[178,"`session` merges the WebView's `document.cookie`, `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` with the newest captured `Cookie` header (httpOnly cookies are